1
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:38,220
Yeah! Woo! Oh, the audio is doubled! Ahhh!

2
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:48,220
Both are coming through! It's doubled! It's doubled! Ahhhh!

3
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:53,530
Yesterday I might've had a chill time with Azuki, but that's not happening today.

4
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:55,930
I can't afford to take it easy.

5
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,750
Should be fine though, right?

6
00:00:57,750 --> 00:01:03,070
I really can't take it easy here.

7
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:03,830
Phew.

8
00:01:03,830 --> 00:01:07,620
Forgot—

9
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:09,020
Forgot—

10
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,520
It's been a while since Polka's last stream,

11
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:12,780
so I should give a recap.

12
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:15,780
So, today we're going tank hunting with Luna.

13
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:16,920
Yep.

14
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,380
Yep, that's it.

15
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:19,160
That's the recap?

16
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:20,940
That was literally everything.

17
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:23,620
That's the recap?

18
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:28,700
Ahaha, that's the recap!

19
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:34,300
Recover missiles, hazmat suit—

20
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:37,190
It's a mess in here.

21
00:01:37,190 --> 00:01:41,750
I made a bunch more missile ammo and added it here.

22
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:44,510
3, 4, 12... twelve of them.

23
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:47,390
Let's take more.

24
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:51,270
I missed a lot yesterday. Shooting from this range is tough.

25
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:55,070
Didn't hit anything?

26
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:56,870
Couldn't hit it?

27
00:01:56,870 --> 00:01:58,670
Couldn't hit it at all.

28
00:01:58,670 --> 00:02:03,800
More food, more food.

29
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,800
Food's decent enough.

30
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,800
The helmet is just way too—

31
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:11,600
Tank Dismantling Center!

32
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:15,400
We're dismantling tanks, so... Tank Hamburg Steak!

33
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,400
Delicious~

34
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:20,200
It's become such a proper little shop now.

35
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:22,000
Isn't that a shop too?

36
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
You're right!

37
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,800
It's turned into a shop.

38
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,800
The shop that Ponpon built—

39
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,600
Made quite a bit of money with this.

40
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,400
Myself included.

41
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,200
We still have 5000 scrap though?

42
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:36,200
Still 5000 scrap?

43
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:39,000
Yeah, what are we gonna do with all this?

44
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Wait, didn't we use a lot yesterday?

45
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,800
We didn't really use as much as I thought.

46
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:53,420
Hmm... we'd have to burn through 5000 in the evening session. Hmm.

47
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:57,980
5000 scrap just sitting there, what a waste.

48
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:07,980
It's actually increased somehow— oh wait, I added to it. There were times Polka added more... materials piling up, and before you know it Polka's hoarding scrap like crazy.

49
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:14,700
Like some kind of scrap demon! Seriously, how much are you stockpiling?!

50
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:18,960
We should all practice the big helicopter or something—

51
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:22,460
Like, we'd all have to be riding the big heli constantly, otherwise we can't keep up.

52
00:03:22,460 --> 00:03:25,600
Riding the big heli — as a way to spend money—

53
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:30,260
We can't buy a tank, can we? Should we buy a tank?

54
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:31,860
Can we buy one? At the garage?

55
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:33,860
Buying a tank would be hilarious.

56
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:36,960
That's... quite the idea.

57
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:42,870
Hmm~

58
00:03:42,870 --> 00:03:43,870
Alright, let's go.

59
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:46,750
Let's go— huh?

60
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:49,770
Might as well make one.

61
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:52,370
Here, take this!

62
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:54,910
Okay, and...

63
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:57,550
It turned to night!

64
00:03:57,550 --> 00:04:00,070
Tonight~

65
00:04:00,070 --> 00:04:00,930
Is this morning?

66
00:04:00,930 --> 00:04:01,630
Or night?

67
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:03,630
Wait, is this going to be nighttime? This?

68
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:09,150
It's turning to night,

69
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:11,710
so let's wait until it gets bright before heading out.

70
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:16,110
Is the camper van okay? It hasn't decayed, has it?

71
00:04:16,110 --> 00:04:17,750
It hasn't decayed.

72
00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:22,090
Maybe one vehicle is more than enough now?

73
00:04:22,090 --> 00:04:25,690
So there's a chance we could manage with just this one?

74
00:04:25,690 --> 00:04:26,790
Exactly.

75
00:04:26,790 --> 00:04:31,210
But hey, don't underestimate me — this is Polka you're talking about.

76
00:04:31,210 --> 00:04:34,690
Just because Azuki-chi taught me a bunch of stuff yesterday doesn't mean—

77
00:04:34,690 --> 00:04:35,870
That's fair, honestly.

78
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:38,930
Right? You're kind of underestimating me there.

79
00:04:38,930 --> 00:04:41,970
Ponpon, your gold bag is sticking out!

80
00:04:41,970 --> 00:04:43,390


81
00:04:43,390 --> 00:04:48,930
No matter how much you teach me...

82
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:50,850
Oh, it's glowing

83
00:04:50,850 --> 00:04:54,360
Gold

84
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:57,400
Luna's worried about us being on our own over here

85
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,200


86
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,360
That doesn't make any sense

87
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:01,600
Normally there'd be someone protecting the princess

88
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,200
But the princess is fine on her own?

89
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,000
What's going on?

90
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,460
Well, we were totally fine yesterday though

91
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:09,460
Polka is really trusted, huh

92
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:11,500
Paradoxical

93
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:14,300
Seriously, yesterday we were way too close to the tank

94
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:16,320
Yeah, that's true

95
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:18,060
It was right near Kachu's place

96
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:20,860
Yeah, apparently we didn't need to be that close

97
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:22,100
Right, right, right

98
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:23,790
Hmm

99
00:05:23,790 --> 00:05:24,620
Hmm

100
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:29,770
If something good drops today

101
00:05:29,770 --> 00:05:30,650
That'd be a win

102
00:05:30,650 --> 00:05:32,270
Well, destroying the tank is already a win

103
00:05:32,270 --> 00:05:34,870
Oh, but like

104
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:36,470
The items—

105
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:42,510
Apparently rare drops include the L96 and M249.

106
00:05:42,510 --> 00:05:47,310
It's gotta be the M249. The M249.

107
00:05:47,310 --> 00:05:50,110
So the M249 or something could drop.

108
00:05:50,110 --> 00:05:54,110
We still haven't gotten it, and it's probably Kanatan's dream too.

109
00:05:54,110 --> 00:05:56,910
Oh right, we really haven't gotten it.

110
00:05:56,910 --> 00:06:02,910
Yeah. Kanatan's always been like "I want it!" about the M249.

111
00:06:04,710 --> 00:06:06,110
The only one we haven't gotten is the black one

112
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:08,710
Right, we got the black one

113
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:10,310
So we're going for the M249

114
00:06:10,310 --> 00:06:12,710
If the M249 drops, we'll probably be at peace

115
00:06:12,710 --> 00:06:14,410
Yeah, we'll finally be at peace

116
00:06:14,410 --> 00:06:14,910
Hmm

117
00:06:14,910 --> 00:06:17,110
Everyone will be at peace

118
00:06:17,110 --> 00:06:17,710
Hmm

119
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:22,990
And we'll get to see just how powerful it is

120
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:25,790
Will it drop? Will it drop?

121
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:27,290
I'm gonna eat this

122
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:29,290
Tasty

123
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:32,990
Yesterday I was totally freaking out, but

124
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:34,990
Now I feel totally relaxed

125
00:06:34,990 --> 00:06:37,980
Wait, is that a flag?

126
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,400
We've got this in the bag

127
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,200
Just do it!

128
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:41,960
We've got this

129
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:45,600
Do it! Do the Easter egg hunt!

130
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:46,220
Huh?

131
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:49,080
But there's a helicopter flying around

132
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,320
Yeah, that's scary

133
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:54,490
Just go without a basket, Usami

134
00:06:54,490 --> 00:06:56,410
There's a helicopter out there

135
00:06:56,410 --> 00:06:58,410
Wait, what?

136
00:06:58,410 --> 00:07:01,410
I can even hear animal sounds nearby.

137
00:07:01,410 --> 00:07:07,700
Is anyone here?

138
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:14,540
Seems like there might be someone.

139
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:21,470
Got one.

140
00:07:21,470 --> 00:07:23,470
If we're gonna go one-two, now's the time.

141
00:07:23,470 --> 00:07:26,270
It's just the two of us here.

142
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:28,270
We could get 3 silver eggs from this

143
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:29,740
True

144
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:32,150
Oh, we get 3?

145
00:07:32,150 --> 00:07:34,650
Yeah, if we're in first place with no one else around

146
00:07:34,650 --> 00:07:37,650
We'd probably get like 3 silver eggs

147
00:07:37,650 --> 00:07:39,150
Wow, that many?

148
00:07:39,150 --> 00:07:40,140
What's this

149
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:41,450
This one—

150
00:07:41,450 --> 00:07:44,750
First place — can I get first with just one?

151
00:07:44,750 --> 00:07:46,460
Nice

152
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:47,350
Nice

153
00:07:47,350 --> 00:07:50,150
Oh, but Polka's slower so

154
00:07:50,150 --> 00:07:52,150
Polka ends up in second place, by the scoring

155
00:07:52,950 --> 00:07:54,950
So there's no first place by win rate?

156
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:59,500
Ha ha ha

157
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:01,300
Ha ha ha

158
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:02,300
Lunch yet?

159
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:04,100
Here's lunch

160
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:07,100
When the cannon comes, you do a crab walk

161
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:09,900
Wait, tell me about that!

162
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:11,700
The crab walk?

163
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:12,700
Yeah.

164
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,500
When the cannon comes—

165
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:17,300
it just blasts you over and over, right?

166
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:19,100
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

167
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:26,840
If you just strafe in one direction when the cannon fires, you can dodge it.

168
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:30,800
That's what you two said yesterday too — so strafing sideways is the way to go.

169
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:33,020
Yeah, yeah! We were doing the same thing.

170
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:34,840
Ooh, pro advice!

171
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:36,340
Step on it.

172
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:38,440
Sideways, yeah, sideways.

173
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:45,220
Sideways — don't move back and forth, just keep going in one direction.

174
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:48,020
Do the crab! Do the crab!

175
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:57,820
Think we can pull it off?

176
00:08:57,820 --> 00:09:02,820
Of course we can! Wait, is the bed still there?

177
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:06,620
I'll go camping style.

178
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:10,400
It's there! The spot where I died yesterday is clearly marked.

179
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:14,820
Alright, let's head out.

180
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:15,760
Let's go!

181
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:16,620
They're going already—

182
00:09:16,620 --> 00:09:17,620
Getting excited now, huh?

183
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:18,620
Let's go!

184
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:20,420
Yep.

185
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:21,220
Oh, are you coming out?

186
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:22,220
Yep.

187
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:24,020
Oh right—

188
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:25,020
Should we take one vehicle?

189
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:25,820
Hmm?

190
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:26,620
Or two?

191
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:27,620
Let's take two, just in case.

192
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:28,620
Two vehicles.

193
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:31,420
We've got plenty of room though.

194
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:32,420
Honestly, one's fine.

195
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:33,420
Ah, fair enough.

196
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:34,420
Then one's fine.

197
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:36,220
I'm counting on you.

198
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:39,990
Alright!

199
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:41,790
We're way too chill about this.

200
00:09:43,090 --> 00:09:45,090
Yeah, we're way too relaxed.

201
00:09:45,090 --> 00:09:47,890
It'll probably be fine, I think.

202
00:09:47,890 --> 00:09:49,690
After it was over yesterday too—

203
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:51,690
Oh wait, there was only one.

204
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:56,490
She probably took down like 5 or 6 tanks off-stream yesterday. We'll be fine.

205
00:09:56,490 --> 00:09:57,290
Eggs!

206
00:09:57,290 --> 00:09:59,290
Eggs showed up? Hold on—

207
00:09:59,290 --> 00:10:01,290
Wait, Polka's getting left behind too!

208
00:10:01,290 --> 00:10:03,090
Why are you doing the same thing?

209
00:10:03,090 --> 00:10:05,090
Three eggs showed up!

210
00:10:05,090 --> 00:10:06,890
With these—

211
00:10:06,890 --> 00:10:10,490
Got it placed!

212
00:10:10,490 --> 00:10:13,340
How do you get off?

213
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:15,180
You can get off with Space, right?

214
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:18,340
You can get off with Space, normally.

215
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:23,110
There's no day you can't get off with Space, right?

216
00:10:23,110 --> 00:10:26,890
Why can't you get off?

217
00:10:26,890 --> 00:10:36,820
Did Space suddenly break?

218
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:41,260
Like, if you move the car a little more, you can get in the passenger seat?

219
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:43,180
That's not a thing, is it?

220
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:47,500
You can't get stuck in the passenger seat, right?

221
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:50,480
Hold on.

222
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,120
I can't get in.

223
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:53,830
What?

224
00:10:53,830 --> 00:10:56,910
The prompt to get in isn't showing up. Why?

225
00:10:56,910 --> 00:11:01,360
Push, push!

226
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:04,510
Push!

227
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:04,810
Huh?

228
00:11:04,810 --> 00:11:06,310
Push!

229
00:11:06,310 --> 00:11:08,430
Got it!

230
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:10,170
Must've been a bad angle.

231
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:11,170
Bad timing.

232
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:12,960
Exactly.

233
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:15,180
That was close!

234
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:18,420
Polka broke out in a cold sweat there!

235
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:24,820
There's a helicopter kind of flying around.

236
00:11:30,030 --> 00:11:33,220
Oh come on—

237
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:35,830
It's kind of heading this way though.

238
00:11:35,830 --> 00:11:39,530
It's right on the road we need to take.

239
00:11:39,530 --> 00:11:41,870
And we're the only ones around—

240
00:11:42,050 --> 00:11:48,910
They're definitely targeting us!

241
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:50,320
Obviously.

242
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:55,530
Like, "now's our chance to take down the heli" kind of vibe.

243
00:11:55,530 --> 00:11:56,870
We're definitely gonna get shot.

244
00:11:56,870 --> 00:11:58,050
They ignored us.

245
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,590
They ignored us.

246
00:11:59,590 --> 00:12:02,870
Are we okay?

247
00:12:02,870 --> 00:12:03,550
We're fine.

248
00:12:03,550 --> 00:12:11,820
Supply drop coming down right now.

249
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:14,180
That's close.

250
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:16,600
Do we even need more supplies?

251
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:23,190
Indiscriminate attack incoming!

252
00:12:23,190 --> 00:12:29,550
I'm a law-abiding citizen!

253
00:12:29,550 --> 00:12:31,350
Wh-wh-what?!

254
00:12:31,350 --> 00:12:34,770
A citizen?

255
00:12:34,770 --> 00:12:36,570
Wait, Makkuru?

256
00:12:36,570 --> 00:12:37,570
Wha, it just keeps—

257
00:12:37,570 --> 00:12:40,690


258
00:12:40,690 --> 00:12:43,410
What the hell!

259
00:12:43,410 --> 00:12:46,290
Hey, stop with the real stuff!

260
00:12:46,290 --> 00:12:49,090
Missiles?! Are you kidding me?!

261
00:12:49,090 --> 00:12:51,890
Don't you dare fly off looking all satisfied!

262
00:12:51,890 --> 00:12:54,690
Hey!

263
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:55,690
Hey!

264
00:12:56,490 --> 00:12:59,250
We still have to eat after this, you know!

265
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:02,870
Unbelievable.

266
00:13:02,870 --> 00:13:11,200
That guy looked so satisfied.

267
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:14,160
Hey, the car's completely wrecked!

268
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:20,160
Why?!

269
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:28,350
The car...

270
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:31,410
This makes no sense, why?!

271
00:13:31,410 --> 00:13:34,530
Is the stuff still inside? Can we not get it out?

272
00:13:34,970 --> 00:13:36,830
Wait, seriously? No way.

273
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:37,890
I don't know.

274
00:13:37,890 --> 00:13:39,390
Push, push!

275
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:40,650
Push, push!

276
00:13:40,650 --> 00:13:44,340
Can you push it?

277
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:47,040
Pushing is all I can do.

278
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:48,820
It really was inside.

279
00:13:48,820 --> 00:13:50,760
Oh right, we were repairing it.

280
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:51,720
Fix it.

281
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,180
Seriously?

282
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:54,080
The square one.

283
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,780
Let me grab the backpack.

284
00:13:55,780 --> 00:14:00,180
What even is this?

285
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:04,730
I feel like it's coming back again.

286
00:14:04,770 --> 00:14:07,710
I can hear it.

287
00:14:07,710 --> 00:14:10,510
What is going on?

288
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:16,170
Oh, it drops at Hangan.

289
00:14:16,170 --> 00:14:17,970
Oh, both of them went down too.

290
00:14:17,970 --> 00:14:19,770
They're our allies!

291
00:14:19,770 --> 00:14:21,760
Both of them are dead.

292
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:23,370
That's weird.

293
00:14:23,370 --> 00:14:27,370
Five seconds ago it felt like we had it in the bag.

294
00:14:27,370 --> 00:14:31,770
Polka, you're quite the entertainer, aren't you?

295
00:14:31,770 --> 00:14:32,770
If you put it nicely.

296
00:14:32,770 --> 00:14:35,570
If you put it nicely, yeah, an entertainer.

297
00:14:35,570 --> 00:14:39,520
We need to do something.

298
00:14:45,790 --> 00:14:47,590
My heart's suddenly pounding.

299
00:14:47,590 --> 00:14:49,390
My heart's suddenly pounding.

300
00:14:49,390 --> 00:14:51,390
Wait, can we even repair it?

301
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,020
There's a Bushi.

302
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:53,990
True.

303
00:14:53,990 --> 00:14:55,990
Bushi is super close.

304
00:14:55,990 --> 00:15:00,770
Are there residents or something there?

305
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:02,370
Yeah.

306
00:15:02,370 --> 00:15:05,010
If we can repair it—

307
00:15:05,010 --> 00:15:08,610
We'd want to get the stuff out of it.

308
00:15:08,610 --> 00:15:11,370
Polka had a lot in there, like hazmat suits.

309
00:15:11,370 --> 00:15:13,370
I'll go grab the airdrop.

310
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:16,660
The airdrop's close.

311
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:18,260
Wait, did it break?

312
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,060
Huh?

313
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:20,660
What?

314
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:22,660
The stuff inside~~

315
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:26,460
Hey, banging on it won't fix it.

316
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:28,260
Oh, oh, the stuff inside—

317
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,540
The stuff inside!

318
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:31,080
Oh no.

319
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:31,700
Oh no.

320
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,940
"Oh no" — that's kind of funny.

321
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:34,680
Oh my.

322
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:37,200
Now I can only push.

323
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:37,700
Oh no.

324
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:39,260
Both hands—

325
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:40,980
Give them back!

326
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:41,900
Hmm.

327
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:46,060
It might be a bad spot.

328
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:48,440
Same old lineup.

329
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:51,360
But pushing doesn't change anything.

330
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:52,880
No way.

331
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:55,580
It's gone.

332
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:58,620
Wait, so we can't even knock on it anymore?

333
00:15:58,620 --> 00:16:01,100
Right, and we can't take out the fuel either.

334
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:02,740
So it's broken then.

335
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:03,940
It's broken.

336
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:06,100
Wow, it can actually break.

337
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:10,520
No way!

338
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:14,350
Oh no!

339
00:16:14,350 --> 00:16:16,750
Whoa! What did we put in it?

340
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:20,560
Tea, like tea stuff — Polka put tea in it.

341
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:24,430


342
00:16:24,430 --> 00:16:26,230
It's over!

343
00:16:26,230 --> 00:16:29,030
There's no getting that back!

344
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:31,030
Actually, I had two ready for exactly this situation.

345
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:33,030
That's why!

346
00:16:33,030 --> 00:16:35,030
That's exactly why!

347
00:16:35,030 --> 00:16:37,830
It was prepared for this moment all along!

348
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:40,630
Can you believe it?

349
00:16:40,630 --> 00:16:43,280
What a coincidence, huh.

350
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:46,230
And we were so well prepared too!

351
00:16:48,030 --> 00:16:51,030
But it's fine — actually better on Polka's end.

352
00:16:51,030 --> 00:16:54,690
Eh, either way—

353
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:57,430
About the same amount of materials—

354
00:16:57,430 --> 00:16:59,430
Gone.

355
00:16:59,430 --> 00:17:05,170
Well, Polka might not have put much in to begin with.

356
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:08,990
I'm starting to think I didn't put anything in.

357
00:17:08,990 --> 00:17:10,670
Well, today—

358
00:17:10,670 --> 00:17:13,590
We're using everything up today anyway, so it's fine.

359
00:17:16,690 --> 00:17:17,690
Alright then.

360
00:17:17,690 --> 00:17:24,090
Wait, that thing Polka was treasuring — the one Luna gave her—

361
00:17:24,090 --> 00:17:27,060
That whatchamacallit thing.

362
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:28,830
Hm?

363
00:17:28,830 --> 00:17:30,690
Whatchamacallit?

364
00:17:30,690 --> 00:17:32,490
Yeah, the important gun.

365
00:17:32,490 --> 00:17:34,290
Where did it go?

366
00:17:34,290 --> 00:17:35,290
Did you see it?

367
00:17:35,290 --> 00:17:37,090
The whatchamacallit?

368
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:39,090
It's the N39, but—

369
00:17:39,090 --> 00:17:40,890
All of it, um—

370
00:17:40,890 --> 00:17:43,810
The attachments were removed.

371
00:17:44,690 --> 00:17:46,690
Whatever, I'll just borrow this one.

372
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:47,190
Alright.

373
00:17:47,190 --> 00:17:48,990
OK.

374
00:17:48,990 --> 00:17:51,470
Yep.

375
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:56,460
We're good.

376
00:17:56,460 --> 00:18:00,260
All things considered, we're fine.

377
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:03,950
Once this heli breaks— wait, it's not a heli.

378
00:18:03,950 --> 00:18:05,860
Once this car breaks, that's it.

379
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:09,160
There are horses!

380
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:12,460
I was thinking yesterday — there are horses here too.

381
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:14,260
There are horses!

382
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,900
There are some right now.

383
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:22,330
I'd rather have the camper van though.

384
00:18:22,330 --> 00:18:26,850
Pumpkin pie — Psycho had a lot of that stocked up.

385
00:18:26,850 --> 00:18:27,590
She had a ton.

386
00:18:27,590 --> 00:18:28,510
But it's fine.

387
00:18:28,510 --> 00:18:30,010
The camper van didn't have much storage anyway.

388
00:18:30,010 --> 00:18:32,670
The camper van side.

389
00:18:32,670 --> 00:18:36,350
Apparently you can get stuff out by scrapping the car.

390
00:18:36,350 --> 00:18:36,930
Really?

391
00:18:36,930 --> 00:18:38,550
We could've broken it.

392
00:18:38,550 --> 00:18:42,580
For real?

393
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:45,840
So we break the car before dismantling the tank?

394
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:47,600
Wait, we're breaking it?

395
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:50,660
There was a rumor that stuff comes out if you break it.

396
00:18:50,660 --> 00:18:53,140
It's not breaking at all!

397
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:57,170
It won't break? It can't break any further?

398
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:58,260
It's done.

399
00:18:58,260 --> 00:19:03,550
Put it on the lift... no wait, we don't have enough lift capacity.

400
00:19:03,550 --> 00:19:05,840
We can't even drive this thing.

401
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:07,490
It's gonna be night again soon.

402
00:19:07,490 --> 00:19:08,590


403
00:19:08,590 --> 00:19:09,830
That's true!

404
00:19:09,830 --> 00:19:16,040
I can't be dealing with this anymore!

405
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:17,540
Let's go!

406
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:21,680
Oh no, Polka's been targeted for like 30 seconds now!

407
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:24,910
30 seconds?

408
00:19:24,910 --> 00:19:25,650
30 seconds.

409
00:19:25,650 --> 00:19:28,050
Oh, probably because I used the Jackhammer just now.

410
00:19:28,050 --> 00:19:31,650
Yeah, just the Jackhammer and it won't forgive me. That's rough.

411
00:19:31,650 --> 00:19:36,530
Maybe we should head over there and wait till morning.

412
00:19:36,530 --> 00:19:38,370
Riverge, Riverge.

413
00:19:39,820 --> 00:19:43,300
Booner.

414
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:49,760
We've thrown away our stuff so many times

415
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:54,660
that we're totally used to losing things by now.

416
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:58,720
We're used to losing things. That was rough.

417
00:19:58,720 --> 00:20:01,000
Ugh, so annoying.

418
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,920
Alright.

419
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:06,930


420
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,900
"We passed through here so many times yesterday."

421
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:14,700
"Yeah."

422
00:20:14,700 --> 00:20:17,120
"Mmhm."

423
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:19,120
"Oh, the gate came off."

424
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:20,920
"Huh, the bumpy one?"

425
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,920
"The straight bumpy one."

426
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,920
"Right side."

427
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:26,720
"Yep."

428
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:28,520
"Rattle rattle."

429
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,320
"Mimin."

430
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:32,320
"Pew pew pew pew pew~"

431
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:36,120
"I wonder if the tank's there."

432
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:37,920
"Is it possible the tank's not there?"

433
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:39,920
It's fine though, there's no exclamation mark.

434
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:42,720
Oh really? Then maybe we're good?

435
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:45,520
Hello there, Mr. Tank~

436
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:49,840
Whoa~

437
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:51,640
Whoa~

438
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:56,400
Yesterday, Azu-chan showed me — you come in from the right side

439
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:57,240
Hey hey hey.

440
00:20:57,240 --> 00:21:02,040
Okay, so first checkpoint?

441
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:09,190
I can hear a bear, but should I just ignore it?

442
00:21:10,190 --> 00:21:15,030
We need to reserve our spot with the tank first.

443
00:21:15,030 --> 00:21:16,940
Right, right.

444
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:23,860
Okay, we're here.

445
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:26,380
The tank just casually comes through

446
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:27,340
along this road.

447
00:21:27,340 --> 00:21:28,640
We made it this far.

448
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:31,360
Was it around here?

449
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:33,720
More towards the front.

450
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:37,640
Don't say it like it's uncertain.

451
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:38,640
The way you're talking about it—

452
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:41,240
I'm gonna die.

453
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:44,040
Say it like it's a definite fact.

454
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:45,840
I'm gonna die!

455
00:21:45,840 --> 00:21:47,440
Can you hear it?

456
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,240
Let's go.

457
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:51,240
There it is, there it is — you scared me!

458
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:55,950
Whereabouts was it again?

459
00:21:55,950 --> 00:21:58,750
Stop saying "whereabouts was it again," stop it.

460
00:21:58,750 --> 00:21:59,750
Whereabouts was it again?

461
00:21:59,750 --> 00:22:01,750
Stop saying "again," stop it.

462
00:22:01,750 --> 00:22:04,560
Stop saying "again."

463
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:06,560
No wait, where was that thing?

464
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:08,360
Wait, suddenly—

465
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:11,360
Huh? Was there a little hill like this here?

466
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:12,360
Don't just suddenly do that, okay?

467
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,960
Una-chan.

468
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:14,960
Una-chan?

469
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:17,760
Una-chan, don't just suddenly do stuff like that.

470
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:21,640
Oh, but, uh, ah, around here, around here.

471
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:23,240
Okay okay okay okay.

472
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:25,240
It was around here.

473
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:29,040
And when the cannon fires, you dodge to the side like this.

474
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:30,910
Ohhh.

475
00:22:30,910 --> 00:22:33,790
But I don't hear the tank yet?

476
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:35,640
Wait, is it here?

477
00:22:36,440 --> 00:22:38,240
It's gotta be here somewhere.

478
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:40,140
Where is it?

479
00:22:40,140 --> 00:22:44,140
All I hear are peaceful sounds.

480
00:22:44,140 --> 00:22:50,740
Yesterday too, we heard it after we'd gone pretty far in.

481
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:53,540
Ah, true. Maybe further in?

482
00:22:53,540 --> 00:22:56,540
But isn't this their home turf?

483
00:22:56,540 --> 00:22:59,340
If I hear a sound, I'll engage.

484
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:02,910
Anyone there?

485
00:23:02,910 --> 00:23:04,750
There's gotta be something here.

486
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:08,170
If there wasn't, there'd be an explosion marker.

487
00:23:08,170 --> 00:23:13,720
It's so peaceful though...

488
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:15,260
Let's go a bit further.

489
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:17,960
Going in.

490
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:20,980
This is a little scary.

491
00:23:20,980 --> 00:23:23,280
I can see myself repeating yesterday's disaster.

492
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:25,720
Oh, the BGM kicked in!

493
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:28,500
Now we're talking.

494
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:32,800
Something's gotta be here.

495
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:36,950
Maybe it just hasn't respawned yet?

496
00:23:36,950 --> 00:23:40,130
Sounds like NPC footsteps.

497
00:23:40,130 --> 00:23:41,210
Hm? Is that an animal?

498
00:23:41,210 --> 00:23:44,140
There are bears here.

499
00:23:44,140 --> 00:23:44,740
A bear, huh.

500
00:23:44,740 --> 00:23:51,370
This is where I kept getting stuck yesterday.

501
00:23:51,370 --> 00:23:54,030
Anything here?

502
00:23:54,030 --> 00:23:59,150
Wake up already! Come on, tank!

503
00:23:59,150 --> 00:24:01,350
Is it not here?

504
00:24:01,350 --> 00:24:06,950
There was a tank around here yesterday...

505
00:24:06,950 --> 00:24:10,190
Isn't that the entrance over there?

506
00:24:10,190 --> 00:24:15,230
You can hear that "eee" sound, right? Yeah, yeah, yeah.

507
00:24:15,230 --> 00:24:20,030
"Oh no." Wait... don't tell me... it's not here?

508
00:24:20,030 --> 00:24:23,430
It's gone? Wait, it's here? Huh?

509
00:24:23,430 --> 00:24:26,030
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

510
00:24:26,030 --> 00:24:29,610
Tank?

511
00:24:29,610 --> 00:24:37,230
No sound at all. Yeah, I don't hear anything.

512
00:24:37,230 --> 00:24:41,230
Has anyone been here within the last hour?

513
00:24:42,030 --> 00:24:44,030
Where'd it go?

514
00:24:44,030 --> 00:24:45,350
Huh? What?

515
00:25:13,550 --> 00:25:15,550
Is there nothing here at all?

516
00:25:15,550 --> 00:25:18,350
I have no idea.

517
00:25:18,350 --> 00:25:20,150
Seriously though...

518
00:25:20,150 --> 00:25:22,950
Is it just the tank, or do people loot everything?

519
00:25:22,950 --> 00:25:24,950
Just the loot inside, right?

520
00:25:24,950 --> 00:25:26,750
It's not here.

521
00:25:26,750 --> 00:25:30,150
Are there any NPC-type enemies?

522
00:25:30,150 --> 00:25:32,150
There are boars.

523
00:25:32,150 --> 00:25:33,950
If it's just boars...

524
00:25:33,950 --> 00:25:35,750
Sorry, there's nothing here!

525
00:25:35,750 --> 00:25:36,750
It's really not here!

526
00:25:36,750 --> 00:25:38,750
Are you kidding me, it's gone!

527
00:25:38,750 --> 00:25:40,750
And I came fully prepared too!

528
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:43,230
It's a tank stream!

529
00:25:43,230 --> 00:25:43,830
Still not here.

530
00:25:43,830 --> 00:25:49,860
If it had been recent at least, I'd have known.

531
00:25:49,860 --> 00:25:51,280
No way.

532
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:52,640
I can't believe it.

533
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:54,580
I can't believe it.

534
00:25:54,580 --> 00:25:56,960
To think it would come to this.

535
00:25:56,960 --> 00:26:01,490
To think it would come to this...

536
00:26:01,490 --> 00:26:04,570
This plan has completely fallen apart.

537
00:26:04,570 --> 00:26:12,740
It's not even wandering around the perimeter.

538
00:26:14,260 --> 00:26:16,260
Because I can't hear any sound at all.

539
00:26:16,260 --> 00:26:23,940
The rooftop spot Aza told me about — is that tricky to use? It's not that high up though.

540
00:26:23,940 --> 00:26:28,460
Ugh... ugh...

541
00:26:28,460 --> 00:26:31,360
Hey, don't go doing a secret tank thing behind the scenes.

542
00:26:31,360 --> 00:26:34,060
A secret tank.

543
00:26:34,060 --> 00:26:36,060
What even is a secret tank.

544
00:26:36,060 --> 00:26:37,060
A secret tank, seriously.

545
00:26:37,060 --> 00:26:39,060
Front stage: Renge. Back stage: tank.

546
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:42,860
Wait, huh?

547
00:26:43,660 --> 00:26:45,500
No sound at all.

548
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:47,520
It's super peaceful.

549
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:51,220
Then what was all that stuff that killed us yesterday?

550
00:26:51,220 --> 00:26:53,920
Maybe there was never a tank here to begin with.

551
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:56,060
Was it a hallucination?

552
00:26:56,060 --> 00:26:57,920
An illusion~

553
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:59,460
It was~

554
00:26:59,460 --> 00:27:01,680
This is ridiculous — when does the tank even spawn?

555
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:03,360
Spawn now, come on!

556
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:05,980
Seriously!

557
00:27:05,980 --> 00:27:09,660
Let me check the rooftop at least.

558
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:14,380
Let me do a quick scout.

559
00:27:14,380 --> 00:27:16,700


560
00:27:16,700 --> 00:27:18,660
Anyone here?

561
00:27:18,660 --> 00:27:21,960
Has anyone recently

562
00:27:21,960 --> 00:27:23,800
taken down

563
00:27:23,800 --> 00:27:25,520
a tank?

564
00:27:25,520 --> 00:27:27,180
That sounded kinda artsy

565
00:27:27,180 --> 00:27:31,420
Ugh, that came out weird

566
00:27:31,420 --> 00:27:32,760
Maybe with a space it'd be

567
00:27:32,760 --> 00:27:34,360
easier to read?

568
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:40,400
Like, "Anyone... space... recently"

569
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:42,240
Ahahahaha

570
00:27:43,700 --> 00:27:45,040
That's terrible

571
00:27:45,040 --> 00:27:48,480
I really should've made a reservation

572
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:49,880
Are you serious?

573
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:55,700
I said everyone would rush the tank on the last day

574
00:27:55,700 --> 00:27:56,900
Polka called it!

575
00:27:56,900 --> 00:28:02,280
I knew the tank would be the most popular attraction today

576
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:02,760
Why though!

577
00:28:02,760 --> 00:28:06,540
We should've written down tank time slots

578
00:28:06,540 --> 00:28:07,420
Reservations

579
00:28:07,420 --> 00:28:09,640
By the hour

580
00:28:09,440 --> 00:28:16,540
Yeah, you needed a reservation — like "tank at what time" — and then Pol and Luna come back together

581
00:28:16,540 --> 00:28:20,500
Oh no, it's over!

582
00:28:20,500 --> 00:28:26,520
Wait, it's done?! Luna already took out the tank?!

583
00:28:26,520 --> 00:28:28,520
Let's go!

584
00:28:28,520 --> 00:28:32,720
Are you kidding me?! There's no one here!

585
00:28:32,720 --> 00:28:40,480
So it was reservation-only, huh?

586
00:28:40,480 --> 00:28:43,600
Really? But if we wait, won't it respawn?

587
00:28:43,600 --> 00:28:49,480
The explosion marker wasn't there, so it must've been before that

588
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:51,840
Maybe it despawned after being scrapped?

589
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:57,380
Even if it despawned after being scrapped, it depends on how long ago that was

590
00:28:57,380 --> 00:28:59,200
How long ago was it?

591
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:02,920
That's why I asked — I want to know the time

592
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:04,800
Maybe there's nobody left at all?

593
00:29:04,800 --> 00:29:05,860
One tank per hour?

594
00:29:05,860 --> 00:29:09,930
So if it's one tank per hour,

595
00:29:09,930 --> 00:29:15,110
if it was an hour ago, would it respawn?

596
00:29:15,110 --> 00:29:16,690
Would it spawn?

597
00:29:16,690 --> 00:29:18,170
If it was an hour ago, then yeah

598
00:29:18,170 --> 00:29:26,130
10...

599
00:29:26,130 --> 00:29:29,430
How long ago was it?

600
00:29:29,430 --> 00:29:34,490
Because ever since I logged in

601
00:29:34,490 --> 00:29:37,430
Pekora's marker wasn't there

602
00:29:37,430 --> 00:29:40,530
Oh really? I wasn't looking at the map

603
00:29:40,530 --> 00:29:47,070
16...

604
00:29:47,070 --> 00:29:51,390
I see

605
00:29:51,630 --> 00:29:53,230
4 PM?

606
00:29:53,230 --> 00:29:55,390
Yeah, around 4:30?

607
00:29:55,390 --> 00:30:01,640
When I checked, it was already fine then

608
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:02,940
So

609
00:30:02,940 --> 00:30:11,540
That means it was before that

610
00:30:11,540 --> 00:30:12,840
Because

611
00:30:12,840 --> 00:30:15,850
Still...

612
00:30:15,850 --> 00:30:17,610
Wait, what?!

613
00:30:17,610 --> 00:30:19,170
Should we wait?

614
00:30:19,170 --> 00:30:21,330
I guess we wait?

615
00:30:21,330 --> 00:30:22,330
If we wait here—

616
00:30:22,330 --> 00:30:29,170
Will it spawn if we wait here? Should we line up just in case?

617
00:30:29,170 --> 00:30:35,010
Excuse me, tank? We're next, sorry!

618
00:30:35,010 --> 00:30:43,070
Next, next, next — we're going for the next tank!

619
00:30:43,070 --> 00:30:45,890
Reservation, queue

620
00:30:45,890 --> 00:30:47,010
Waiting for a reservation

621
00:30:47,010 --> 00:30:48,930
Can we get the next tank? Reservation?

622
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:50,870
Make a reservation for us!

623
00:30:50,870 --> 00:30:52,510
Reserve it!

624
00:30:52,510 --> 00:30:54,250
Alright, let's make a reservation

625
00:30:54,250 --> 00:30:57,250
When it's a once-an-hour attraction,

626
00:30:57,250 --> 00:30:58,850
people

627
00:30:58,850 --> 00:31:02,090
are gonna swarm it

628
00:31:02,090 --> 00:31:03,130
Seems like it

629
00:31:03,130 --> 00:31:03,930
No way

630
00:31:03,930 --> 00:31:05,810
I can't believe it

631
00:31:05,810 --> 00:31:08,610
I didn't think there'd be nobody at this hour

632
00:31:08,610 --> 00:31:10,000
This is bad

633
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:12,260
I don't have a season pass for the tank

634
00:31:12,260 --> 00:31:13,310
Ahh

635
00:31:13,310 --> 00:31:19,950
People are probably doing tank runs back to back — like, wake up and go straight to the tank

636
00:31:19,950 --> 00:31:26,170
I thought we could go right away, same as those pros — but those guys...

637
00:31:26,170 --> 00:31:33,870
Are they even keeping up? Or do they just love the thrill of getting it? I dunno

638
00:31:33,870 --> 00:31:38,550
There's no way you can use all that. Does everyone really want to do the tank that badly?

639
00:31:38,550 --> 00:31:41,290
I heard the tank gives the best loot though

640
00:31:41,290 --> 00:31:42,330
Oh really?

641
00:31:42,330 --> 00:31:45,490
So how was it actually? Did you get good loot yesterday?

642
00:31:45,490 --> 00:31:49,970
Well, I mean... yeah, I guess

643
00:31:49,970 --> 00:31:51,350
Was it good?

644
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:54,670
No rare drops, so I'm not sure

645
00:31:54,670 --> 00:31:56,870
Do rocket launcher ammo drop from it?

646
00:31:56,870 --> 00:32:00,070
Oh yeah, yeah! Ammo did drop, rocket launcher ammo

647
00:32:00,070 --> 00:32:05,550
So it drops rocket launcher ammo so you can go blow up another tank?

648
00:32:05,550 --> 00:32:07,550
It never ends

649
00:32:07,550 --> 00:32:10,970
That's why you can't help but keep farming it

650
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:12,250
I see

651
00:32:12,250 --> 00:32:15,270
I went ahead and made the reservation public

652
00:32:15,270 --> 00:32:16,910
But I did make a reservation this time

653
00:32:16,910 --> 00:32:20,910
People just logging in now definitely won't know about it though

654
00:32:20,910 --> 00:32:25,030
Like, why would you farm at this point?

655
00:32:25,030 --> 00:32:29,150
No no, that's exactly WHY you'd come today

656
00:32:29,150 --> 00:32:29,850
Huh?

657
00:32:29,850 --> 00:32:32,610
People might come specifically because it's today

658
00:32:32,610 --> 00:32:34,890
Ah, like pulling a gacha over and over

659
00:32:34,890 --> 00:32:38,630
Right, and since today's the last day, lots of people want to experience the final tank

660
00:32:38,630 --> 00:32:39,890
The final...

661
00:32:39,890 --> 00:32:42,590
Today is the last day of PvE, after all

662
00:32:42,590 --> 00:32:44,450
One last time

663
00:32:44,450 --> 00:32:48,010
Everyone wants to do a commemorative tank run, I think

664
00:32:48,010 --> 00:32:49,310
That's true

665
00:32:49,310 --> 00:32:50,670
A commemorative tank run

666
00:32:50,670 --> 00:32:53,850
They want to do a commemorative tank farm

667
00:32:53,850 --> 00:32:54,710
Exactly

668
00:32:54,710 --> 00:32:58,790
To explain for anyone just tuning in—

669
00:32:58,790 --> 00:33:00,770
We went to go take down the tank

670
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:03,370
And the tank wasn't there

671
00:33:03,370 --> 00:33:06,560
So right now is the time

672
00:33:06,560 --> 00:33:08,760
We can watch for it

673
00:33:08,760 --> 00:33:11,100
Not sure where it'll be wandering around though

674
00:33:11,100 --> 00:33:12,160
Hard to say

675
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:13,620
I didn't go inside last time

676
00:33:13,620 --> 00:33:16,020
I was shooting from way outside earlier

677
00:33:16,020 --> 00:33:17,140
Yeah, like

678
00:33:17,140 --> 00:33:20,220
Azukichi was probably told to fight it from a distance

679
00:33:20,220 --> 00:33:22,700
Something like that

680
00:33:22,700 --> 00:33:24,080
Yeah yeah, exactly

681
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:29,570
If you think about it as one tank per hour...

682
00:33:29,570 --> 00:33:31,070
That's about 8 more chances

683
00:33:31,070 --> 00:33:32,390
"About 8 more" is kind of funny

684
00:33:32,390 --> 00:33:34,990
All the tank slots might already be reserved

685
00:33:34,990 --> 00:33:36,750
Right, 8 times

686
00:33:36,750 --> 00:33:38,230
First come, first served

687
00:33:38,230 --> 00:33:39,190
Hah

688
00:33:39,190 --> 00:33:41,850
There might be someone out there who's absolutely determined

689
00:33:41,850 --> 00:33:44,150
to claim every single tank

690
00:33:44,150 --> 00:33:45,550
You think?

691
00:33:45,550 --> 00:33:46,790
First come, first served

692
00:33:46,790 --> 00:33:48,430
Hmm, what do you think — around 4 o'clock?

693
00:33:48,430 --> 00:33:49,710
I think it'll spawn around 4

694
00:33:49,710 --> 00:33:50,910
Hmm...

695
00:33:50,910 --> 00:33:53,530
Who took it down and when?

696
00:33:53,530 --> 00:33:59,910
Maybe right after Sora logged in and finished?

697
00:33:59,910 --> 00:34:04,950
It was already done when Polka checked the map

698
00:34:04,950 --> 00:34:10,110
It might spawn again pretty soon

699
00:34:10,110 --> 00:34:15,790
I'm hoping so

700
00:34:15,790 --> 00:34:19,650
Yesterday I was shooting from around here too

701
00:34:19,650 --> 00:34:21,450
I see

702
00:34:21,450 --> 00:34:23,250
So this area works too

703
00:34:23,250 --> 00:34:25,050
Shots incoming

704
00:34:25,050 --> 00:34:27,050
It got stuck over there

705
00:34:27,050 --> 00:34:29,050
Around NE50

706
00:34:29,050 --> 00:34:32,850
So they get stuck too

707
00:34:32,850 --> 00:34:34,850
It was completely stuck and not moving at all

708
00:34:34,850 --> 00:34:36,650
So I was targeting it there

709
00:34:36,650 --> 00:34:40,250
Get stuck again, please

710
00:34:40,250 --> 00:34:42,250
Does an announcement pop up when it spawns?

711
00:34:42,250 --> 00:34:45,850
Yeah, that red notification shows up

712
00:34:47,650 --> 00:34:49,850
Something like "[something] has been dispatched"

713
00:34:49,850 --> 00:34:51,190
What does it say for the tank?

714
00:34:51,190 --> 00:34:52,570
Like CH something?

715
00:34:52,570 --> 00:34:54,930
It shows CH-something, right?

716
00:34:54,930 --> 00:34:59,180
Does it actually say "tank"?

717
00:34:59,180 --> 00:34:59,780
Not sure

718
00:34:59,780 --> 00:35:02,100
What usually shows up is...

719
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:03,700
But there's one I can never figure out

720
00:35:03,700 --> 00:35:04,860
What was it called again

721
00:35:04,860 --> 00:35:08,740
Cargo ship and...

722
00:35:08,740 --> 00:35:10,380
Wait, what was it again?

723
00:35:10,380 --> 00:35:13,340
Is the cargo ship the tank? Could it be?

724
00:35:13,340 --> 00:35:14,100
I wonder...

725
00:35:14,100 --> 00:35:16,360
It kind of sounds like a tank, doesn't it?

726
00:35:16,360 --> 00:35:20,160
"Is Channel CH the transport heli?"

727
00:35:20,160 --> 00:35:21,660
Oh, so there's no tank?

728
00:35:21,660 --> 00:35:23,560
"Ship means a ship"

729
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:26,560
Right, ship is...

730
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:28,160
Get the tank online!

731
00:35:28,160 --> 00:35:31,160
Announce that the tank is online today!

732
00:35:31,160 --> 00:35:33,260
Please get the tank online!

733
00:35:33,260 --> 00:35:36,760
Hey, spawn the tank for us!

734
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:39,060
That's asking a lot...

735
00:35:39,060 --> 00:35:41,060
I want a tank right now!

736
00:35:41,060 --> 00:35:43,160
Give us a tank, please!

737
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:45,160
Spawn like two of them, please!

738
00:35:45,160 --> 00:35:47,460
Bold of you to ask.

739
00:35:47,460 --> 00:35:53,350
When the tank logs in, make a proper announcement!

740
00:35:53,350 --> 00:35:56,740
I wonder if it'll show up...

741
00:35:56,740 --> 00:35:59,540
Should we wait until 4 AM?

742
00:35:59,540 --> 00:36:02,260
That's about all we can do.

743
00:36:02,260 --> 00:36:03,140
With some fun conversation to pass the time.

744
00:36:03,140 --> 00:36:04,140
Yeah, exactly.

745
00:36:04,140 --> 00:36:07,940
So, looking back at the end — how was it?

746
00:36:07,940 --> 00:36:10,740
It went by so fast!

747
00:36:11,540 --> 00:36:18,420
Luna even rearranged her work schedule for this event.

748
00:36:18,420 --> 00:36:27,300
At first I was worried about whether I could set up the farm system in a week...

749
00:36:27,300 --> 00:36:31,620
But overall it went pretty smoothly!

750
00:36:32,840 --> 00:36:39,840
In the second half, Polka helped out and we got a ton of pumpkins too.

751
00:36:39,840 --> 00:36:46,640
I never imagined I'd end up taking care of pumpkins myself either.

752
00:36:46,640 --> 00:36:51,240
Truly. We worked on it together.

753
00:36:51,240 --> 00:36:55,840
She's already doing the closing.

754
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:59,180
Closing first — a pre-booked closing.

755
00:36:59,180 --> 00:37:00,640
Closing, closing!

756
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:02,080
I figured I'd get the closing out of the way early.

757
00:37:02,080 --> 00:37:05,520
The order's all over the place today.

758
00:37:05,520 --> 00:37:07,940
Like, might as well do the closing first.

759
00:37:07,940 --> 00:37:11,340
Starting with the closing remarks.

760
00:37:11,340 --> 00:37:13,340
What kind of stream starts with the closing remarks?

761
00:37:13,340 --> 00:37:18,060
Are there any other interesting things to do here besides the tank?

762
00:37:18,060 --> 00:37:21,120
Hmm... not really.

763
00:37:21,120 --> 00:37:27,720
I heard there's a recycler if you use the scrap...

764
00:37:27,720 --> 00:37:33,360
I want something fun to do — there's nothing here.

765
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:40,700
It's getting dark. Once it's night, it's lonely, cold, and confusing.

766
00:37:40,700 --> 00:37:45,040
We'll have no choice but to go back to the camper. Let's camp in the camper!

767
00:37:45,040 --> 00:37:46,840
Let's camp!

768
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:48,640
Should we shoot down the heli?

769
00:37:48,640 --> 00:37:52,440
Can we even do that?

770
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:54,240
I don't really know how to take down the heli either.

771
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:58,040
If you picked up meat—

772
00:37:58,040 --> 00:38:00,040
Cook it in the camper!

773
00:38:00,040 --> 00:38:03,840
Meat, right.

774
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:05,640
But I don't have any wood.

775
00:38:05,640 --> 00:38:07,640
I brought wood!

776
00:38:07,640 --> 00:38:09,640
Then cook the meat!

777
00:38:09,640 --> 00:38:11,440
If we can cook in the camper—

778
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:13,440
Can you actually cook in the camper?

779
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:15,240
The camper door opened!

780
00:38:15,240 --> 00:38:17,240
Where did we park the car again?

781
00:38:17,240 --> 00:38:19,040
Over there.

782
00:38:19,040 --> 00:38:22,690
The camper's open!

783
00:38:22,690 --> 00:38:24,440
Right here.

784
00:38:24,440 --> 00:38:26,270
Should we camp out here?

785
00:38:26,270 --> 00:38:32,240
Can we cook here?

786
00:38:32,240 --> 00:38:34,950
Oh, we can!

787
00:38:42,560 --> 00:38:45,960
Isn't it dangerous to cook inside the car?

788
00:38:45,960 --> 00:38:49,760
That's just what campers are for!

789
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:53,990
We're gonna get carbon monoxide poisoning.

790
00:38:53,990 --> 00:38:57,790
Open a window!

791
00:38:57,790 --> 00:38:59,590
We'll get carbon monoxide poisoning!

792
00:38:59,590 --> 00:39:01,390
Open the window!

793
00:39:01,390 --> 00:39:03,390
All windows are sealed shut.

794
00:39:03,390 --> 00:39:07,620
That's actually scary.

795
00:39:09,620 --> 00:39:13,280
That's raw meat though.

796
00:39:13,280 --> 00:39:14,440
Didn't pick any up?

797
00:39:14,440 --> 00:39:16,380
I didn't bring any meat.

798
00:39:16,380 --> 00:39:19,300
Just cooking nothing.

799
00:39:19,300 --> 00:39:23,260
Oh, you're getting ammo right now.

800
00:39:23,260 --> 00:39:24,440
Getting ammo.

801
00:39:24,440 --> 00:39:26,860
I accidentally threw a grenade

802
00:39:26,860 --> 00:39:28,520
Why did you throw a grenade?

803
00:39:28,520 --> 00:39:31,260
Stop it!

804
00:39:31,260 --> 00:39:32,980
Inside the car—

805
00:39:32,980 --> 00:39:34,780
Please don't throw grenades in the car!

806
00:39:34,780 --> 00:39:36,980
I thought we exploded

807
00:39:36,980 --> 00:39:38,780
Hehehe~

808
00:39:38,780 --> 00:39:40,580
Good luck!

809
00:39:40,580 --> 00:39:43,580
It's way too peaceful here... will it actually spawn?

810
00:39:43,580 --> 00:39:45,380
Hehehe~

811
00:39:45,380 --> 00:39:50,180
I wonder if it's tied to real-world time or something

812
00:39:50,180 --> 00:39:51,980
I don't know, how does it work?

813
00:39:51,980 --> 00:39:53,780
Hm, oh!

814
00:39:53,780 --> 00:39:55,580
Oh, that startled me

815
00:39:55,580 --> 00:39:56,580
Wait, what?

816
00:39:56,580 --> 00:39:59,380
That was just a car outside in real life

817
00:39:59,380 --> 00:40:01,180
Did it spawn?

818
00:40:01,180 --> 00:40:02,980
Hmm, not sure

819
00:40:02,980 --> 00:40:09,780
A tank has spawned near Polka too

820
00:40:09,780 --> 00:40:14,850
It's going to be nighttime soon

821
00:40:14,850 --> 00:40:16,850
No no no no

822
00:40:16,850 --> 00:40:24,210
Night is a bit dangerous, I'll do it once it's daytime

823
00:40:24,210 --> 00:40:29,810
You can see the fire from outside too

824
00:40:30,670 --> 00:40:32,610
The detail is incredible

825
00:40:32,610 --> 00:40:36,410
Polka is indoors

826
00:40:36,410 --> 00:40:39,350
making charcoal

827
00:40:39,350 --> 00:40:42,150
She's making charcoal right now

828
00:40:42,150 --> 00:40:44,950
So, how is it? Are you hearing anything?

829
00:40:44,950 --> 00:40:48,750
I mean, we're literally inside

830
00:40:48,750 --> 00:40:50,550
the enemy's

831
00:40:50,550 --> 00:40:54,350
base, so it could spawn any time, right?

832
00:40:54,350 --> 00:40:58,150
This car might get blown up too

833
00:40:59,150 --> 00:41:03,860
I don't hear anything at all

834
00:41:03,860 --> 00:41:11,220
Maybe it hasn't respawned yet

835
00:41:11,220 --> 00:41:15,120
There's still 5 minutes until it shows up

836
00:41:15,120 --> 00:41:16,680
It's probably still being built right now

837
00:41:16,680 --> 00:41:18,840
Most likely

838
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:21,200
I hope it's being built

839
00:41:21,200 --> 00:41:25,720
We just can't seem to get a good fight

840
00:41:25,720 --> 00:41:28,120
against the tank

841
00:41:28,120 --> 00:41:29,000
We've been at this

842
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:31,400
since yesterday

843
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:33,960
Yeah, that's true

844
00:41:33,960 --> 00:41:38,040
Polka said Luna taught her, so I'm looking forward to seeing it

845
00:41:38,040 --> 00:41:40,460
For real though

846
00:41:40,460 --> 00:41:45,300
I figured we'd get to see her in action today, but the timing just isn't working out

847
00:41:45,300 --> 00:41:47,960
The timing just isn't lining up

848
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:50,640
Is it because I lit a fire? My comfort level went up

849
00:41:50,640 --> 00:41:53,260
It was at 50% yesterday

850
00:41:53,260 --> 00:41:55,460
It's comfortable in here

851
00:41:55,460 --> 00:41:57,040
Yeah

852
00:41:57,040 --> 00:41:58,700
This is comfortable?

853
00:41:59,600 --> 00:42:03,600
I checked the airdrop, but

854
00:42:03,600 --> 00:42:08,770
what about our tank?

855
00:42:08,770 --> 00:42:11,420
Can you check on the tank too?

856
00:42:11,420 --> 00:42:13,420
Still being manufactured

857
00:42:13,420 --> 00:42:17,040
Does it spawn from above like a dinosaur in ARK?

858
00:42:17,040 --> 00:42:19,020
Who knows

859
00:42:19,020 --> 00:42:21,020
A tank... hmm

860
00:42:21,020 --> 00:42:24,820
We started with that explosion drop after all

861
00:42:26,420 --> 00:42:30,680
Yesterday was crazy — it was basically a zombie attack

862
00:42:30,680 --> 00:42:34,280
That was totally unnecessary

863
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:40,530
It's night. Yeah, it's nighttime

864
00:42:40,530 --> 00:42:44,810
Hurry up and spawn already

865
00:42:44,810 --> 00:42:52,300
Instagram notification

866
00:42:52,300 --> 00:42:56,300
I have to check Instagram no matter what — oh, morning

867
00:42:56,300 --> 00:43:01,670
Does it spawn here? It's spawning, it's spawning!

868
00:43:01,670 --> 00:43:03,070
Let's split the tanks!

869
00:43:03,070 --> 00:43:04,710
Seriously

870
00:43:04,710 --> 00:43:05,430
Did you crack an egg?

871
00:43:05,430 --> 00:43:08,190
Wait, isn't this a once-per-hour event?

872
00:43:08,190 --> 00:43:08,870
Right?

873
00:43:08,870 --> 00:43:11,510
If so, I thought an hour had already passed

874
00:43:11,510 --> 00:43:15,970
Or does it mean one hour after you defeat it?

875
00:43:15,970 --> 00:43:17,470
Oh, Easter?

876
00:43:17,470 --> 00:43:19,170
Right, is Easter once per hour?

877
00:43:19,170 --> 00:43:20,870
How does Easter work exactly?

878
00:43:20,870 --> 00:43:22,970
If so, an hour has passed

879
00:43:22,970 --> 00:43:25,570
Timing-wise it's been about an hour though

880
00:43:25,570 --> 00:43:26,270
Right?

881
00:43:28,220 --> 00:43:36,020
The worst case would be if we're doing eggs near the tank spawn and a tank suddenly appears and just unloads on us.

882
00:43:36,020 --> 00:43:36,820
True.

883
00:43:36,820 --> 00:43:39,820
Which one is whose, anyway?

884
00:43:39,820 --> 00:43:44,050
Is it not here?

885
00:43:44,050 --> 00:43:47,860
No tank?

886
00:43:47,860 --> 00:43:51,100
Is that a helicopter?

887
00:43:51,100 --> 00:43:53,900
That's not a tank sound.

888
00:43:53,900 --> 00:43:58,000
Why isn't it here?

889
00:43:58,000 --> 00:44:01,220
The tank had a much more aggressive sound to it.

890
00:44:01,220 --> 00:44:03,820
What is that sound then?

891
00:44:03,820 --> 00:44:06,920
That's probably just something flying overhead.

892
00:44:06,920 --> 00:44:08,000
Something flying overhead?

893
00:44:08,000 --> 00:44:17,600
Even the first time I heard the tank, I could tell it meant business.

894
00:44:17,600 --> 00:44:18,420
Yeah.

895
00:44:18,420 --> 00:44:22,000
Even on first listen, that sound had pure killing intent.

896
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:24,040
Should we go look for it again?

897
00:44:25,640 --> 00:44:28,880
But when we came here before, the tank was already here.

898
00:44:28,880 --> 00:44:29,820
It was here, right? Yesterday?

899
00:44:29,820 --> 00:44:31,060
It was here, right?

900
00:44:31,060 --> 00:44:31,840
We were taking it down.

901
00:44:31,840 --> 00:44:33,600
How did the practice run go yesterday?

902
00:44:33,600 --> 00:44:38,500
We took it down in practice too.

903
00:44:38,500 --> 00:44:45,500
I mean, this is literally the tank's route.

904
00:44:45,500 --> 00:44:47,840
It'd be weird if it wasn't here.

905
00:44:47,840 --> 00:44:54,530
Exactly.

906
00:44:54,530 --> 00:44:56,990


907
00:44:56,990 --> 00:44:59,710
Is there like a thing where you can't tell unless you move away?

908
00:44:59,710 --> 00:45:01,370


909
00:45:01,370 --> 00:45:03,570
Yeah, maybe being right here means you can't tell.

910
00:45:03,570 --> 00:45:04,730
Because like, the whole time

911
00:45:04,730 --> 00:45:07,930
we've been getting notifications like "spawned" and stuff.

912
00:45:07,930 --> 00:45:10,650
So I don't think that's the case.

913
00:45:10,650 --> 00:45:11,750
Hmm, I wonder...

914
00:45:11,750 --> 00:45:13,010
Ponpon, Unatan.

915
00:45:13,010 --> 00:45:13,830
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

916
00:45:13,830 --> 00:45:16,760
Oh, oh, uh, okay.

917
00:45:16,760 --> 00:45:21,450
Sorry.

918
00:45:21,450 --> 00:45:22,590
So, Polka has to

919
00:45:22,590 --> 00:45:26,410
step away for a bit tonight.

920
00:45:26,410 --> 00:45:29,310
Right during prime time,

921
00:45:29,310 --> 00:45:31,410
I can't be here for prime time,

922
00:45:31,410 --> 00:45:32,790
so it ended up being this time slot.

923
00:45:32,790 --> 00:45:35,770
But when I come back,

924
00:45:35,770 --> 00:45:44,850
today is still PvE until midnight,

925
00:45:44,850 --> 00:45:47,390
and apparently the server's open,

926
00:45:47,390 --> 00:45:50,170
so I'm hoping to stream again if I can.

927
00:45:50,170 --> 00:45:51,130
Polka too.

928
00:45:51,130 --> 00:45:54,400
I think Kanatan feels the same.

929
00:45:54,400 --> 00:45:56,000
Why?

930
00:45:56,000 --> 00:45:58,300
Let's enjoy it

931
00:45:58,300 --> 00:46:03,130
to the very end.

932
00:46:03,130 --> 00:46:03,830
Anyway,

933
00:46:03,830 --> 00:46:06,810
the tank hasn't respawned yet.

934
00:46:06,810 --> 00:46:07,910
Okaaay.

935
00:46:07,910 --> 00:46:10,570
Polka has really been

936
00:46:10,570 --> 00:46:14,010
in Luna's care a lot this time around,

937
00:46:14,010 --> 00:46:15,330
and Kanatan too—

938
00:46:15,330 --> 00:46:18,410
probably more than I even realize.

939
00:46:18,410 --> 00:46:22,590
But in return, it's been so much fun.

940
00:46:22,590 --> 00:46:28,090
Thank you so much for having us.

941
00:46:28,090 --> 00:46:37,790
I'm not sure what'll happen during PvP,

942
00:46:37,790 --> 00:46:40,830
but for Polka, getting to stay with Luna

943
00:46:40,830 --> 00:46:48,110
really showed me how fun this can be.

944
00:46:48,110 --> 00:46:51,830
When I was alone going "I have no idea what I'm doing,"

945
00:46:51,830 --> 00:46:55,350
Luna invited me to live with her,

946
00:46:55,350 --> 00:46:56,820
so, um...

947
00:46:56,820 --> 00:46:57,750
I'm really grateful—

948
00:46:57,750 --> 00:46:59,030
It's here!

949
00:46:59,030 --> 00:47:01,590
Luna's here!

950
00:47:01,590 --> 00:47:06,340
Luna, where are you?!

951
00:47:06,340 --> 00:47:08,540
It's coming!

952
00:47:08,540 --> 00:47:10,380
The tank is here?!

953
00:47:10,180 --> 00:47:12,180
What's going on?

954
00:47:12,180 --> 00:47:19,540
What's happening?

955
00:47:19,540 --> 00:47:26,920
Luna, the tank is here!

956
00:47:26,920 --> 00:47:28,280
Wait, hold on— what? Did it spawn?

957
00:47:28,070 --> 00:47:28,990
It spawned?!

958
00:47:28,990 --> 00:47:32,520
Wait, I'm dead.

959
00:47:32,320 --> 00:47:35,320
WHAT?! Huh? What? What? What?

960
00:47:35,320 --> 00:47:40,320
I haven't even gone to the bathroom yet — can you please not die?!

961
00:47:40,320 --> 00:47:42,320
Oh wow, there's a red Luna!

962
00:47:42,320 --> 00:47:46,320
Are you kidding me?!

963
00:47:46,320 --> 00:47:52,320
Hey Luna! Luna? Luna? Luna, didn't you set up a bed here?

964
00:47:52,320 --> 00:47:56,320
Ah! Wait, the bathroom... Ah!

965
00:47:56,320 --> 00:47:59,320
What do I do? Luna? Ah!

966
00:47:59,320 --> 00:48:01,320
Blue arrow!

967
00:48:01,120 --> 00:48:03,120
What am I supposed to do?

968
00:48:03,120 --> 00:48:05,120
Why though?!

969
00:48:05,120 --> 00:48:07,120


970
00:48:07,120 --> 00:48:09,120
Huh?

971
00:48:09,120 --> 00:48:11,120
Why now of all times?!

972
00:48:11,120 --> 00:48:13,120
Huh?

973
00:48:13,120 --> 00:48:15,120


974
00:48:15,120 --> 00:48:17,120
Huh?

975
00:48:17,120 --> 00:48:19,120


976
00:48:19,120 --> 00:48:21,120
I wasn't even doing anything!

977
00:48:21,120 --> 00:48:23,120
I didn't do anything either!

978
00:48:26,270 --> 00:48:29,520
I was just sitting at the main camp and got hit by a missile and died!

979
00:48:29,320 --> 00:48:33,720
The tank did its job, but... I didn't even hear the tank though.

980
00:48:33,510 --> 00:48:34,870
Huh, why~?

981
00:48:34,870 --> 00:48:38,470
Huh? I was just telling Luna how much she'd taken care of Polka—

982
00:48:38,470 --> 00:48:41,470
—like, it was really great, you know?

983
00:48:41,470 --> 00:48:44,270
Huh? I hadn't respawned yet.

984
00:48:44,270 --> 00:48:46,870
I come back and I'm dead?!

985
00:48:46,870 --> 00:48:52,510
Hey viewers, seriously, please stop ghosting.

986
00:48:52,510 --> 00:48:54,470
You were watching the stream, right?

987
00:48:54,470 --> 00:48:56,270
Stop ghosting, okay?

988
00:48:56,270 --> 00:48:57,270
I tried timing it.

989
00:48:57,270 --> 00:49:00,270
There's an airdrop that looks like it landed really close by.

990
00:49:02,070 --> 00:49:04,070
Ugh, why did I die? Come on...

991
00:49:04,070 --> 00:49:04,570
Huh?

992
00:49:04,570 --> 00:49:05,570
Seriously?

993
00:49:05,570 --> 00:49:06,870
Can you come here?

994
00:49:06,870 --> 00:49:08,870
Like, should we split things up in the car?

995
00:49:08,870 --> 00:49:11,470
No, the car—

996
00:49:11,470 --> 00:49:14,470
It's not registered so nothing shows up.

997
00:49:14,470 --> 00:49:15,470
The bed—

998
00:49:15,470 --> 00:49:18,270
So, what does Polka have?

999
00:49:18,270 --> 00:49:20,270
Should I go there? Where exactly?

1000
00:49:20,270 --> 00:49:24,070
I think there's a sleeping bag around J-7.

1001
00:49:24,070 --> 00:49:26,870
J-7?

1002
00:49:26,870 --> 00:49:28,670
Yeah, yeah, that's right.

1003
00:49:28,670 --> 00:49:31,070
Somewhere around the same place as yesterday.

1004
00:49:31,070 --> 00:49:34,630
Huh? It said I could set this as my own bed, so probably—

1005
00:49:34,630 --> 00:49:38,210
Hey Luna, right now—

1006
00:49:38,210 --> 00:49:40,710
In the car, Polka—

1007
00:49:40,710 --> 00:49:42,510
I set it as your bed, how's that?

1008
00:49:42,510 --> 00:49:45,570
But it's grayed out and I can't select it.

1009
00:49:45,570 --> 00:49:47,670
Why? It says it's in use.

1010
00:49:47,670 --> 00:49:49,570
I just got out and tried—

1011
00:49:49,570 --> 00:49:51,010
Oh, it showed up! Okay okay okay!

1012
00:49:51,010 --> 00:49:53,130
This one.

1013
00:49:53,130 --> 00:49:54,010
And clothes—

1014
00:49:54,010 --> 00:49:59,650
Clothes are in the top, go ahead and put them on!

1015
00:49:59,650 --> 00:50:04,870
No hazmat suit in here— top, top, top, the closet!

1016
00:50:04,870 --> 00:50:09,250
Where? Top, top, top— found it!

1017
00:50:09,250 --> 00:50:12,670
I thought I was gonna die— well, I did die.

1018
00:50:12,670 --> 00:50:22,470
Hey wait, isn't this awful? Getting attacked while I'm in the bathroom is the worst, right? Did you eat? Did you eat?

1019
00:50:22,470 --> 00:50:24,470
I haven't eaten.

1020
00:50:24,470 --> 00:50:28,470
Can you please stop attacking me while I'm in the bathroom?

1021
00:50:28,470 --> 00:50:35,470
But where were you? Weren't you pretty beat up too?

1022
00:50:35,470 --> 00:50:41,070
I mean, at the very end, so suddenly—

1023
00:50:41,070 --> 00:50:47,070
Going to the bathroom right at the last moment like that probably wasn't the best idea.

1024
00:50:47,070 --> 00:50:50,070
I didn't think they'd show up!

1025
00:50:50,070 --> 00:50:52,790
That scared me!

1026
00:50:52,790 --> 00:50:56,060
I want to go recover my stuff—

1027
00:50:56,060 --> 00:51:00,030
Oh, okay, it's fine, I'll come with you, I'll come with you.

1028
00:51:00,030 --> 00:51:02,590
Wait, wait, I want to go get my stuff back.

1029
00:51:02,590 --> 00:51:04,300
This is the worst.

1030
00:51:04,300 --> 00:51:05,870
That's hilarious.

1031
00:51:05,870 --> 00:51:08,870
That guy knew exactly what he was doing.

1032
00:51:08,870 --> 00:51:11,310
What is going on?

1033
00:51:11,310 --> 00:51:13,750
Why did they suddenly spawn?

1034
00:51:13,750 --> 00:51:18,120
It's just the timer.

1035
00:51:18,320 --> 00:51:20,320
Where's my stuff? Where did it drop?

1036
00:51:20,320 --> 00:51:23,120
Ah, I can hear it!

1037
00:51:23,120 --> 00:51:28,000
Wait, I need to eat some rat-something to recover.

1038
00:51:28,000 --> 00:51:29,800
Okay okay okay.

1039
00:51:29,800 --> 00:51:32,870
Wait, the rat-whatever—

1040
00:51:32,870 --> 00:51:34,870
You dropped it!

1041
00:51:34,870 --> 00:51:38,450
Alright, with this—

1042
00:51:38,450 --> 00:51:40,250
I'll drink some water too.

1043
00:51:40,250 --> 00:51:44,050
Actually I had tea, so I'm good on water.

1044
00:51:46,240 --> 00:51:48,480
Man, seriously, seriously...

1045
00:51:48,480 --> 00:51:51,860
Huh? I missed the moment it got destroyed!

1046
00:51:51,860 --> 00:51:55,080
Luna probably saw it, right?

1047
00:51:55,080 --> 00:52:00,700
But I had the Escape menu open, so...

1048
00:52:00,700 --> 00:52:03,780
What did it look like when it happened?

1049
00:52:03,780 --> 00:52:06,700
Polka was busy setting up a dramatic emotional moment too.

1050
00:52:06,700 --> 00:52:07,160
Oh no...

1051
00:52:07,160 --> 00:52:09,060
Apparently I only heard the sound.

1052
00:52:09,060 --> 00:52:12,740
I should've told you to get somewhere safe beforehand.

1053
00:52:12,740 --> 00:52:18,240
I totally thought it wasn't coming yet, like at all.

1054
00:52:18,240 --> 00:52:19,560
You'd think it wasn't coming, right?

1055
00:52:19,560 --> 00:52:23,220
Luna's all beat up — you practiced yesterday, didn't you?

1056
00:52:23,220 --> 00:52:25,280
I mean, come on—

1057
00:52:25,280 --> 00:52:27,200
You should've practiced taking a bathroom break too!

1058
00:52:27,200 --> 00:52:29,860
I wasn't even there!

1059
00:52:29,860 --> 00:52:32,840
Seriously, where did I die?

1060
00:52:32,840 --> 00:52:36,510
Is Hen-chan around?

1061
00:52:36,510 --> 00:52:39,710
Yeah, I hear sounds from the N direction.

1062
00:52:39,710 --> 00:52:42,930
Polka's body should be somewhere around here.

1063
00:52:42,930 --> 00:52:45,170
Found it! I died here.

1064
00:52:45,170 --> 00:52:48,290
There's a death marker here.

1065
00:52:48,290 --> 00:52:52,970
Good, that spot looks safe.

1066
00:52:52,970 --> 00:52:55,850
Grab it quick!

1067
00:52:55,850 --> 00:52:58,170
Not hearing much right now.

1068
00:52:58,170 --> 00:53:01,130
It's N direction, but I can still hear something.

1069
00:53:01,130 --> 00:53:06,470
Let me fall back and sort through my stuff.

1070
00:53:06,470 --> 00:53:07,810
It's moving away.

1071
00:53:07,810 --> 00:53:09,690
But it's definitely coming this way.

1072
00:53:09,690 --> 00:53:10,750
This is so scary...

1073
00:53:10,750 --> 00:53:12,850
Man, I can't believe this...

1074
00:53:12,850 --> 00:53:18,650
Don't do anything funny!

1075
00:53:18,650 --> 00:53:21,460
Why did you open the options menu?!

1076
00:53:21,460 --> 00:53:24,670
It doesn't matter what screen it was!

1077
00:53:24,670 --> 00:53:27,680
Let me see how you died!

1078
00:53:27,680 --> 00:53:29,350
I had it on a different screen—

1079
00:53:29,350 --> 00:53:31,790
I walked right past it with the Escape menu still open.

1080
00:53:31,790 --> 00:53:33,410
Ugh!

1081
00:53:33,410 --> 00:53:36,770
It shouldn't matter what screen you're on!

1082
00:53:37,930 --> 00:53:40,170
Well, at least you respawned, so it's fine.

1083
00:53:40,170 --> 00:53:41,170
Yeah, true.

1084
00:53:41,170 --> 00:53:44,410
Okay, with this—

1085
00:53:44,410 --> 00:53:46,350
We can do this!

1086
00:53:46,350 --> 00:53:47,430
Where is it?

1087
00:53:47,430 --> 00:53:50,410
Luna, where did you go?

1088
00:53:50,410 --> 00:53:52,110
I'm already inside — wait, I'm in!

1089
00:53:52,110 --> 00:53:52,970
What?!

1090
00:53:52,970 --> 00:53:57,780
Yesterday I was around here with Azu-chan and the others—

1091
00:53:57,780 --> 00:53:59,060
You went all the way there?

1092
00:53:59,060 --> 00:54:01,940
From around here, on the right side—

1093
00:54:01,940 --> 00:54:05,180
There's a good spot near the entrance, you know?

1094
00:54:06,580 --> 00:54:07,580
Is it here?

1095
00:54:07,580 --> 00:54:11,200
Yes, yes, yes — I can hear it clearly!

1096
00:54:11,200 --> 00:54:14,820
Oh no, is Polka closer? NW—

1097
00:54:14,820 --> 00:54:16,360
N, NW.

1098
00:54:16,360 --> 00:54:20,220
I can hear it — it's here, it's here! Visual, visual, visual!

1099
00:54:20,220 --> 00:54:24,180
Visual, NW, N.

1100
00:54:24,180 --> 00:54:25,300
340.

1101
00:54:25,300 --> 00:54:29,800
NW, this way?

1102
00:54:29,800 --> 00:54:32,440
I see the tank!

1103
00:54:34,270 --> 00:54:37,070


1104
00:54:37,070 --> 00:54:39,350
From here—

1105
00:54:39,350 --> 00:54:42,750
Where, where, where did it go? Where do I hit it from?

1106
00:54:42,750 --> 00:54:44,250
N.

1107
00:54:44,250 --> 00:54:48,900
Hold on, Polka might be closer to it.

1108
00:54:48,900 --> 00:54:51,320
You're pretty far out there — is that spot okay?

1109
00:54:51,320 --> 00:54:54,760
No! Visual, visual, visual over there!

1110
00:54:54,760 --> 00:55:00,240
For now, I just shot at it!

1111
00:55:00,240 --> 00:55:08,540
Got it, got it, got it! Crab, crab, crab! Crab crab! Couldn't do it — crab! Scary scary scary! Crab crab crab!

1112
00:55:08,540 --> 00:55:14,400
You're drawing a ton of aggro! It's doing some kind of scissor attack right now.

1113
00:55:14,400 --> 00:55:20,800
The hate's going your way so I can shoot freely — oh no oh no! I've got the aggro!

1114
00:55:20,800 --> 00:55:26,400
Crab crab crab crab crab — I can't even see the tank, where is it?

1115
00:55:26,400 --> 00:55:28,400
Huh? N... N20... Oh, there it is!

1116
00:55:28,400 --> 00:55:35,970
Crab crab crab crab... It wouldn't walk through here, right?

1117
00:55:35,970 --> 00:55:38,770
Crab crab crab crab...

1118
00:55:38,770 --> 00:55:42,270
After all that firing, even the enemy should have a cooldown, right?

1119
00:55:42,270 --> 00:55:44,070
No it doesn't!

1120
00:55:44,070 --> 00:55:45,870
It's right in front of me!

1121
00:55:45,870 --> 00:55:47,670
Kanata?

1122
00:55:47,670 --> 00:55:49,170
She was right in front of me

1123
00:55:49,170 --> 00:55:50,970
Are you shooting? Yeah, yeah, shooting

1124
00:55:50,970 --> 00:55:52,770
She was just way too close

1125
00:55:52,770 --> 00:55:55,770
Kanata, where are you? You're too far forward!

1126
00:55:55,770 --> 00:55:57,770
Pull back!

1127
00:55:57,770 --> 00:56:00,570
Get further back!

1128
00:56:00,570 --> 00:56:02,370
Why are you there?!

1129
00:56:02,370 --> 00:56:05,600
Why did you die there?!

1130
00:56:05,600 --> 00:56:07,400
Come over here!

1131
00:56:07,400 --> 00:56:10,960
Ah! Polka's bed!

1132
00:56:10,960 --> 00:56:15,470
I died!

1133
00:56:15,470 --> 00:56:17,270
She's dead!

1134
00:56:17,270 --> 00:56:19,100
I died!

1135
00:56:19,100 --> 00:56:22,070
You can't be that close! Come over here, over here!

1136
00:56:22,070 --> 00:56:25,670
And now I'm dead too!

1137
00:56:25,670 --> 00:56:27,670
Is there a bed somewhere? Is there a bed?

1138
00:56:27,670 --> 00:56:29,470
Oh no, it's far

1139
00:56:29,470 --> 00:56:32,270
Now the fight against radiation begins

1140
00:56:32,270 --> 00:56:37,070
Let me head back and drop off the suit

1141
00:56:37,070 --> 00:56:43,030
Or just give me a bed

1142
00:56:43,030 --> 00:56:46,430
You can give me the camper van bed

1143
00:56:46,430 --> 00:56:50,230
Hold on, I'm heading back to the camper van

1144
00:56:50,230 --> 00:56:55,030
The cannon's firing

1145
00:56:55,830 --> 00:56:58,830
Wait, the camper van was pretty far back

1146
00:56:58,830 --> 00:57:08,120
The camper van...

1147
00:57:08,120 --> 00:57:09,920
Yeah, I knew it

1148
00:57:09,920 --> 00:57:12,720
Ow ow ow, I'm getting shot

1149
00:57:12,720 --> 00:57:16,520
Practice and the real thing with Polka are totally different

1150
00:57:16,520 --> 00:57:18,320
It's intense

1151
00:57:19,200 --> 00:57:25,360
Next time, stay about 150 meters back

1152
00:57:25,360 --> 00:57:27,840
Yeah, it's intense

1153
00:57:27,840 --> 00:57:31,560
Polka's also on edge from the boar sounds right now

1154
00:57:31,560 --> 00:57:34,380
Can I give this sleeping bag to a friend?

1155
00:57:34,380 --> 00:57:35,140
Yeah, yeah, go ahead

1156
00:57:35,140 --> 00:57:37,840
Oh, an airdrop!

1157
00:57:37,840 --> 00:57:39,220
Thank you

1158
00:57:39,220 --> 00:57:42,240
Let me return one suit too

1159
00:57:42,240 --> 00:57:44,080
There's a hazmat suit here

1160
00:57:44,080 --> 00:57:46,320
There isn't

1161
00:57:46,320 --> 00:57:51,900
Can I do it here?

1162
00:57:51,900 --> 00:57:56,500
Oh, right

1163
00:57:56,500 --> 00:57:58,300
Is it dangerous here? Should I move back?

1164
00:57:58,300 --> 00:58:01,900
What do I do? Respawn? What was it again?

1165
00:58:01,900 --> 00:58:04,700
Do I just go down here?

1166
00:58:04,700 --> 00:58:07,500
I can't move

1167
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:11,300
Do I just die here? What am I supposed to do?

1168
00:58:11,300 --> 00:58:14,100
I'm so confused

1169
00:58:14,100 --> 00:58:15,780
Respawn, right?

1170
00:58:15,780 --> 00:58:16,760
Okay

1171
00:58:16,760 --> 00:58:20,920
That's pretty far

1172
00:58:20,920 --> 00:58:24,740
The tank is actually pretty close to this car

1173
00:58:24,740 --> 00:58:25,880
That's what

1174
00:58:25,880 --> 00:58:27,780
messed me up

1175
00:58:27,780 --> 00:58:31,670
I misjudged

1176
00:58:31,670 --> 00:58:32,790
the distance to the tank

1177
00:58:32,790 --> 00:58:36,790
How about around here?

1178
00:58:36,790 --> 00:58:38,750
Found it, found it

1179
00:58:38,750 --> 00:58:40,190
There we go

1180
00:58:40,190 --> 00:58:40,950
With this

1181
00:58:40,950 --> 00:58:45,050
So, how's that?

1182
00:58:45,050 --> 00:58:47,850
Alright, heading out

1183
00:58:47,850 --> 00:58:53,740
Where am I spawning?

1184
00:58:53,740 --> 00:58:56,040
You'll spawn right there

1185
00:58:56,040 --> 00:58:58,340
Okay, I ended up way far away

1186
00:58:58,340 --> 00:58:59,640
Hello

1187
00:58:59,640 --> 00:59:00,640
I'm far

1188
00:59:00,640 --> 00:59:05,240
I went up to a small hill

1189
00:59:05,240 --> 00:59:06,240
Taking damage

1190
00:59:07,840 --> 00:59:10,220
A small hill

1191
00:59:10,220 --> 00:59:12,760
There should be a hazmat suit there too

1192
00:59:12,760 --> 00:59:16,000
Thank you!

1193
00:59:16,000 --> 00:59:16,980
Una

1194
00:59:16,980 --> 00:59:18,760
It's Una

1195
00:59:18,760 --> 00:59:21,920
A sleeping bag... but this is a high-traffic area so I can't place it

1196
00:59:21,920 --> 00:59:22,680
Oh, food

1197
00:59:22,680 --> 00:59:24,960
For sure

1198
00:59:24,960 --> 00:59:26,980
Oh, there's a pumpkin

1199
00:59:26,980 --> 00:59:29,440
Give me the pumpkin

1200
00:59:29,440 --> 00:59:31,140
Hey hey hey

1201
00:59:31,140 --> 00:59:34,420
Thanks!

1202
00:59:34,420 --> 00:59:39,720
If you go a little further back from where Polka was earlier, you'll be fine.

1203
00:59:39,720 --> 00:59:41,980
Is this it? I feel like I'm not hitting it.

1204
00:59:41,980 --> 00:59:43,680
Not at all.

1205
00:59:43,680 --> 00:59:45,680
Yeah, can't hit it — it's too far.

1206
00:59:45,680 --> 00:59:50,320
Right?

1207
00:59:50,320 --> 00:59:51,720
Alright!

1208
00:59:51,720 --> 00:59:53,460
Good thing the tank spawned.

1209
00:59:53,460 --> 00:59:55,560
Yeah, lucky!

1210
00:59:55,560 --> 00:59:57,820
Good thing we reserved it.

1211
00:59:57,820 --> 01:00:01,420
Turns out it was a tank you couldn't get without a reservation.

1212
01:00:01,420 --> 01:00:04,720
It showed up out of nowhere though.

1213
01:00:04,720 --> 01:00:05,820
True.

1214
01:00:05,820 --> 01:00:08,180
I really want some kind of heads-up that it's coming.

1215
01:00:08,180 --> 01:00:12,760
Heave-ho.

1216
01:00:12,760 --> 01:00:13,760
Heave-ho.

1217
01:00:13,760 --> 01:00:14,740
Heave-ho.

1218
01:00:14,740 --> 01:00:15,160
Heave-ho.

1219
01:00:15,160 --> 01:00:16,040
Heave-ho.

1220
01:00:16,040 --> 01:00:17,070
Heave-ho.

1221
01:00:17,070 --> 01:00:18,600
For the tank too,

1222
01:00:18,600 --> 01:00:19,800
ideally,

1223
01:00:19,800 --> 01:00:22,060
like with the helicopter — "it's currently moving through this area"

1224
01:00:22,060 --> 01:00:23,600
something like that would be nice.

1225
01:00:23,600 --> 01:00:25,900
There's nothing like that.

1226
01:00:25,900 --> 01:00:27,040
Kani-chan!

1227
01:00:27,040 --> 01:00:27,600
Kani-chan.

1228
01:00:27,600 --> 01:00:28,440
Kani-chan, Kani-chan!

1229
01:00:28,440 --> 01:00:29,240
Yeah, yeah.

1230
01:00:29,240 --> 01:00:31,100
And around here, right here—

1231
01:00:31,100 --> 01:00:32,600
Oh! I can hear it!

1232
01:00:34,820 --> 01:00:39,080
Shoot from the front here, then fall back down.

1233
01:00:39,080 --> 01:00:40,720
Yeah, you can hear it — it's coming from inside.

1234
01:00:40,720 --> 01:00:43,000
Break line of sight.

1235
01:00:43,000 --> 01:00:45,000
Break line of sight — right, that's what we need to do.

1236
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:46,780
Matsuri-chan's gonna be annoyed at us.

1237
01:00:46,780 --> 01:00:50,180
We were pushing a bit too far forward — stay around here.

1238
01:00:50,180 --> 01:00:52,260
It's super loud around here.

1239
01:00:52,260 --> 01:00:52,700
Yeah, it is.

1240
01:00:52,700 --> 01:00:55,400
It's coming — visual, visual, visual!

1241
01:00:55,400 --> 01:00:57,540
Fired!

1242
01:00:57,540 --> 01:00:59,400
Ugh, missed.

1243
01:00:59,400 --> 01:01:00,120
It went right past.

1244
01:01:00,120 --> 01:01:03,580
Visual confirmed.

1245
01:01:03,580 --> 01:01:05,580
Why are you eyeballing it?!

1246
01:01:05,580 --> 01:01:08,380
I mean, you can actually see it!

1247
01:01:08,380 --> 01:01:11,340
Polpol?

1248
01:01:11,340 --> 01:01:12,340
I'm running away!

1249
01:01:12,340 --> 01:01:14,140
No way, it's scary!

1250
01:01:14,140 --> 01:01:15,140
Go down!

1251
01:01:15,140 --> 01:01:15,940
Down?

1252
01:01:15,940 --> 01:01:19,270
Over here, over here!

1253
01:01:19,270 --> 01:01:22,870
Wait, where are you, Polpol?

1254
01:01:22,870 --> 01:01:24,670
Down here, inside this.

1255
01:01:24,670 --> 01:01:27,970
Okay, okay, okay!

1256
01:01:27,970 --> 01:01:33,250
I'm in here.

1257
01:01:33,250 --> 01:01:34,250
There you are!

1258
01:01:36,930 --> 01:01:39,490
The Aza-chan route Kanata taught me yesterday.

1259
01:01:39,490 --> 01:01:41,650
Can the tank get in here?

1260
01:01:41,650 --> 01:01:43,870
It can't come in here, so we hide here.

1261
01:01:43,870 --> 01:01:47,550
The tank's still out there...

1262
01:01:47,550 --> 01:01:50,200
It's there!

1263
01:01:50,200 --> 01:01:52,880
Are the NPCs getting more frantic too?

1264
01:01:52,880 --> 01:01:58,220
They're not going crazy, but they're there if you peek out.

1265
01:01:58,220 --> 01:01:59,460
You're right.

1266
01:01:59,460 --> 01:02:04,320
I've never been over this way.

1267
01:02:04,320 --> 01:02:07,440
We're being camped!

1268
01:02:07,580 --> 01:02:09,980
Wait — aren't we trapped like rats?

1269
01:02:09,980 --> 01:02:13,770
Go out another way.

1270
01:02:13,770 --> 01:02:17,570
Ah! Wait! NPCs are coming!

1271
01:02:17,570 --> 01:02:20,370
I don't have a gun! Of all times—

1272
01:02:20,370 --> 01:02:22,170
Oh, there they are.

1273
01:02:22,170 --> 01:02:24,960
I don't have a gun — Nathan, help!

1274
01:02:24,960 --> 01:02:27,770
Apparently if the NPCs break through, you should retreat for now.

1275
01:02:27,770 --> 01:02:28,620
Got it.

1276
01:02:28,620 --> 01:02:30,570
But retreat to where?

1277
01:02:30,570 --> 01:02:32,870
Nathan doesn't really know this map either...

1278
01:02:32,870 --> 01:02:34,870
Oh, I think I got a Pol-hate status.

1279
01:02:37,300 --> 01:02:40,260
Should we go that way? Maybe exit through the Ponpon side?

1280
01:02:40,260 --> 01:02:47,850
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho.

1281
01:02:47,850 --> 01:02:52,370
It's probably around NE direction

1282
01:02:52,370 --> 01:02:54,480
Oh, thanks

1283
01:02:54,480 --> 01:02:55,980
Where did the tank go?

1284
01:02:55,980 --> 01:02:57,570
Tank's that way too

1285
01:02:57,570 --> 01:03:00,970
It's around NE60

1286
01:03:00,970 --> 01:03:02,720
NE60, copy

1287
01:03:02,720 --> 01:03:03,570
That's far

1288
01:03:03,570 --> 01:03:05,870
Alright, let's aim from here

1289
01:03:15,300 --> 01:03:16,380
Not hitting it?

1290
01:03:16,380 --> 01:03:20,920
Tank went back to its original position

1291
01:03:20,920 --> 01:03:24,230
It went in front of the room

1292
01:03:24,230 --> 01:03:25,770
I see

1293
01:03:25,770 --> 01:03:29,430
Where's its original position?

1294
01:03:29,430 --> 01:03:32,810
We gotta go recover Polka's body

1295
01:03:32,810 --> 01:03:33,950
Enemies might spawn

1296
01:03:33,950 --> 01:03:37,560
Huh? Polka's body?

1297
01:03:37,560 --> 01:03:39,100
Oh, it's by that little hill

1298
01:03:39,100 --> 01:03:40,240
Oh, I don't remember

1299
01:03:40,240 --> 01:03:41,200
Where was it again?

1300
01:03:41,200 --> 01:03:42,560
Over there

1301
01:03:42,560 --> 01:03:44,300
The little hill

1302
01:03:44,420 --> 01:03:48,220
The little hill... that's kinda scary

1303
01:03:48,220 --> 01:03:52,020
Yeah, the tank was

1304
01:03:52,020 --> 01:03:54,820
Pretty close by, right?

1305
01:03:54,820 --> 01:03:56,820
Around the M8 marker, thanks

1306
01:03:56,820 --> 01:03:59,670
Looks like we can go now, right?

1307
01:03:59,670 --> 01:04:00,670
Which way?

1308
01:04:00,670 --> 01:04:02,470
Around here? NE40?

1309
01:04:02,470 --> 01:04:06,570
Somewhere around here

1310
01:04:06,570 --> 01:04:08,370
It's around here, right? Let me check

1311
01:04:08,370 --> 01:04:10,510
Hm?

1312
01:04:10,510 --> 01:04:11,510
Wasn't it around here?

1313
01:04:11,510 --> 01:04:12,510
There it is! This, this, this!

1314
01:04:12,510 --> 01:04:13,510
Oh, thanks!

1315
01:04:13,510 --> 01:04:15,110
This, this, this!

1316
01:04:15,110 --> 01:04:17,110
Without this scope I'm totally useless

1317
01:04:17,110 --> 01:04:18,910
Can't see a thing without it

1318
01:04:18,910 --> 01:04:22,510
This spot is too far forward

1319
01:04:22,510 --> 01:04:24,510
Get back, get back!

1320
01:04:24,510 --> 01:04:26,310
Oh, I can hear the tank too

1321
01:04:26,310 --> 01:04:28,110
Can't hear it

1322
01:04:28,110 --> 01:04:30,110
Silence...

1323
01:04:30,110 --> 01:04:31,910
Let's aim from around here

1324
01:04:31,910 --> 01:04:33,910
Once you grab it, fall back

1325
01:04:33,910 --> 01:04:37,580
Got it

1326
01:04:37,580 --> 01:04:39,380
The tank's probably...

1327
01:04:39,380 --> 01:04:41,380
Oh, it's inside the tank

1328
01:04:41,380 --> 01:04:43,680
Yeah, yeah, exactly

1329
01:04:43,680 --> 01:04:46,490
It's right here

1330
01:04:46,490 --> 01:04:48,290
Hm? Oh, is that everyone?

1331
01:04:48,290 --> 01:04:52,390
I was hoping it'd come this way

1332
01:04:52,390 --> 01:04:54,190
Guided? A guided missile?

1333
01:04:54,190 --> 01:04:55,990
Yeah

1334
01:04:55,990 --> 01:05:02,260
It's there!

1335
01:05:02,260 --> 01:05:08,020
Where?

1336
01:05:08,020 --> 01:05:14,910
It's there, but it looks like it might hit the wall

1337
01:05:14,910 --> 01:05:19,640
Which direction?

1338
01:05:20,140 --> 01:05:22,790
Where is it...

1339
01:05:22,790 --> 01:05:25,780
I can hear it but I can't see it

1340
01:05:25,780 --> 01:05:28,390
Oh, there it is! Around N20

1341
01:05:28,390 --> 01:05:30,190
N20, copy

1342
01:05:30,190 --> 01:05:32,190
Shifted right toward N30

1343
01:05:32,190 --> 01:05:34,180
It's in the shadow

1344
01:05:34,180 --> 01:05:41,390
Lost sight of the tank!

1345
01:05:41,390 --> 01:05:45,270
Yesterday the tank wouldn't come out for a while either

1346
01:05:45,270 --> 01:05:47,070
You said it got stuck, right?

1347
01:05:47,070 --> 01:05:50,070
Seemed like it was stuck somewhere

1348
01:05:50,070 --> 01:05:53,870
It got stuck in the second half and we just kept shooting it

1349
01:05:53,870 --> 01:05:57,670
Was there black smoke? Were we hitting it?

1350
01:05:57,670 --> 01:05:58,670
Excellent!

1351
01:05:58,670 --> 01:06:04,450
Oh, there it is! It's there! Around NE50, 40!

1352
01:06:04,450 --> 01:06:05,270
It's there, it's there!

1353
01:06:05,270 --> 01:06:08,070
Come this way!

1354
01:06:08,070 --> 01:06:11,430
It's coming!

1355
01:06:11,430 --> 01:06:13,230
It's coming, it's coming!

1356
01:06:13,230 --> 01:06:16,030
Does a hit sound different somehow?

1357
01:06:16,030 --> 01:06:18,030
Like a sizzling sound

1358
01:06:18,030 --> 01:06:21,430
I want to hear that sound! Oh yeah! Babababababa!

1359
01:06:21,430 --> 01:06:30,120
Ow!

1360
01:06:30,120 --> 01:06:31,120
Whoa! Wha—!

1361
01:06:31,120 --> 01:06:35,920
I wanna hear that sound! Your... crying!

1362
01:06:35,920 --> 01:06:38,220
Oh, that missed...

1363
01:06:38,220 --> 01:06:42,670
Is this sound bad?

1364
01:06:42,670 --> 01:06:46,270
Like a spell... Ow ow ow! It's coming this way!

1365
01:06:46,270 --> 01:06:51,950
Ugh...

1366
01:06:51,950 --> 01:06:53,550
Not at all...

1367
01:06:54,450 --> 01:06:57,510
Wawawawa, my aim is absolute garbage

1368
01:06:57,510 --> 01:07:01,820


1369
01:07:01,820 --> 01:07:04,650
Where? Right now?

1370
01:07:04,650 --> 01:07:08,330
N10... N3... which one is 300?

1371
01:07:08,330 --> 01:07:10,490
I see

1372
01:07:10,490 --> 01:07:15,880
Luna-tan's getting hit by magic fire

1373
01:07:15,880 --> 01:07:19,250
Over there

1374
01:07:19,250 --> 01:07:21,070
Around N10

1375
01:07:21,070 --> 01:07:23,010
It went inside, it went inside!

1376
01:07:23,010 --> 01:07:24,010
Oh no...

1377
01:07:28,860 --> 01:07:32,300
Whoa!

1378
01:07:32,300 --> 01:07:36,820
Getting out from this side is rough

1379
01:07:36,820 --> 01:07:39,020
Can't peek from here either

1380
01:07:39,020 --> 01:07:41,900
Where is it?

1381
01:07:41,900 --> 01:07:45,500
Will it back up?

1382
01:07:45,500 --> 01:07:50,420
Okay, fall back

1383
01:07:50,420 --> 01:07:52,220
Can't see it!

1384
01:07:52,220 --> 01:07:58,660
Enemy soldiers

1385
01:07:58,660 --> 01:08:02,660
Not there, did it go on patrol again?

1386
01:08:03,100 --> 01:08:10,340
Not here either, where'd it go?

1387
01:08:10,340 --> 01:08:12,140
Come on out!

1388
01:08:12,140 --> 01:08:16,050
Oh, but there's one, around N40

1389
01:08:16,050 --> 01:08:19,050
There it is, I can see an eyeball

1390
01:08:19,050 --> 01:08:20,800
Nice

1391
01:08:20,800 --> 01:08:24,650
But it's a bit too far to fire a missile

1392
01:08:24,650 --> 01:08:26,450
Really?

1393
01:08:26,450 --> 01:08:30,390
I can only see its head

1394
01:08:30,390 --> 01:08:32,390
It's hiding~

1395
01:08:32,390 --> 01:08:34,390
Can't see it — is it hiding too?

1396
01:08:34,390 --> 01:08:36,190
It's hiding

1397
01:08:36,190 --> 01:08:37,190
Oh, you're right!

1398
01:08:37,190 --> 01:08:38,990
I can see the eyeball

1399
01:08:38,990 --> 01:08:40,790
Let's just shoot for now

1400
01:08:40,790 --> 01:08:43,790
An airdrop just casually landed

1401
01:08:43,790 --> 01:08:49,770
Hey, isn't it stuck again? That thing

1402
01:08:49,770 --> 01:08:50,770
Oh, then we can just trap it, right?

1403
01:08:50,770 --> 01:08:55,570
I don't know, but even if it's stuck, it'll still attack

1404
01:08:55,570 --> 01:08:56,370
Really?

1405
01:08:56,370 --> 01:08:59,170
We can only dodge by strafing

1406
01:09:03,670 --> 01:09:08,770
You're right, it's trying to move

1407
01:09:08,770 --> 01:09:12,310
Isn't this our chance?

1408
01:09:12,310 --> 01:09:13,530
Hit it

1409
01:09:13,530 --> 01:09:15,650
In the match

1410
01:09:15,650 --> 01:09:17,070
Oh, so close!

1411
01:09:17,070 --> 01:09:18,710
A little too high

1412
01:09:18,710 --> 01:09:25,200
This is hard

1413
01:09:25,200 --> 01:09:27,240
It'll hit

1414
01:09:27,240 --> 01:09:30,600
If it's the same as before

1415
01:09:30,600 --> 01:09:33,040
That thing is seriously stuck

1416
01:09:33,040 --> 01:09:35,340
I think it's probably stuck

1417
01:09:35,340 --> 01:09:36,940
Oh, this is totally not working

1418
01:09:36,940 --> 01:09:42,410
Yeah, it's different after all

1419
01:09:42,410 --> 01:09:46,110
Yeah, it's hard to hit from here

1420
01:09:46,110 --> 01:09:47,210
Oh, too high

1421
01:09:47,210 --> 01:09:48,210
It's right there though

1422
01:09:48,210 --> 01:09:49,710
Too high

1423
01:09:49,710 --> 01:09:51,010
Like a guided missile

1424
01:09:51,010 --> 01:09:53,110
Someone said aim just a tiny bit above

1425
01:09:53,110 --> 01:09:55,210
Just a tiny bit above, is that right?

1426
01:09:55,210 --> 01:10:00,220
It's heading toward Luna

1427
01:10:00,220 --> 01:10:08,540
It's breaking line of sight nicely

1428
01:10:13,540 --> 01:10:15,540


1429
01:10:15,540 --> 01:10:21,900
Oh, did that hit?

1430
01:10:21,900 --> 01:10:23,700
Nice nice! It's on fire!

1431
01:10:23,700 --> 01:10:27,960
It's burning!

1432
01:10:27,960 --> 01:10:30,920
Keep going!

1433
01:10:30,920 --> 01:10:38,230
It's fully targeting Luna, so that's a blessing!

1434
01:10:38,230 --> 01:10:40,030
That hurts!

1435
01:10:40,030 --> 01:10:41,470
Okay, for now...

1436
01:10:41,470 --> 01:10:44,470
I can't see it anymore but it's on fire

1437
01:10:44,470 --> 01:10:53,000
Alright, let's aim again

1438
01:10:54,980 --> 01:10:56,480
Getting close is scary

1439
01:10:56,480 --> 01:10:58,960
Getting close is a bad idea

1440
01:10:58,960 --> 01:11:00,820
This...

1441
01:11:00,820 --> 01:11:04,620
Hope I'm not hitting that weird white wall. Am I okay?

1442
01:11:04,620 --> 01:11:07,380
Did I hit it?

1443
01:11:07,380 --> 01:11:11,300
I keep bumping into this white wall

1444
01:11:11,300 --> 01:11:12,820
I should aim from over here instead

1445
01:11:12,820 --> 01:11:14,220
But the bullets are coming

1446
01:11:14,220 --> 01:11:16,140
I have to strafe to dodge them

1447
01:11:16,140 --> 01:11:19,960
Where is everyone?

1448
01:11:19,960 --> 01:11:24,770
I moved a little off

1449
01:11:25,450 --> 01:11:28,970
Wait, is that a helicopter coming?

1450
01:11:28,970 --> 01:11:30,170
Maybe I'm imagining it

1451
01:11:30,170 --> 01:11:31,450
That thing...

1452
01:11:31,450 --> 01:11:32,830
Up ahead...

1453
01:11:32,830 --> 01:11:39,230
That thing is clearly looking right at us!

1454
01:11:39,230 --> 01:11:42,030
W-w-w-wait wait wait!

1455
01:11:42,030 --> 01:11:44,830
I haven't done anything wrong, please stop!

1456
01:11:44,830 --> 01:11:47,630
I'm a law-abiding citizen!

1457
01:11:47,630 --> 01:11:49,430
Are we okay here?

1458
01:11:49,430 --> 01:11:51,430
Are we okay? It's just really close

1459
01:11:51,430 --> 01:11:53,230
Ow ow ow ow ow!

1460
01:11:53,230 --> 01:11:55,030
Ow ow ow ow ow!

1461
01:11:55,030 --> 01:11:56,830
Ow ow ow ow ow!

1462
01:11:56,830 --> 01:11:58,830
No no no no, I haven't done anything!

1463
01:11:58,830 --> 01:12:00,630
Why?!

1464
01:12:00,630 --> 01:12:03,820
Ow ow ow ow!

1465
01:12:03,820 --> 01:12:05,820
Ow ow ow ow ow!

1466
01:12:05,820 --> 01:12:07,650
Ow ow ow ow ow!

1467
01:12:07,650 --> 01:12:09,620
Why though?!

1468
01:12:09,620 --> 01:12:11,420
This is too brutal

1469
01:12:11,420 --> 01:12:13,220
Indiscriminate attacks, here we go!

1470
01:12:13,220 --> 01:12:15,020
What are we gonna do about the tank?

1471
01:12:15,020 --> 01:12:16,850
The tank is like...

1472
01:12:16,850 --> 01:12:18,820
The tank is here!

1473
01:12:18,820 --> 01:12:23,880
After this, if I somehow recover my health...

1474
01:12:23,880 --> 01:12:25,220
I don't know though

1475
01:12:25,220 --> 01:12:29,060
I don't think I'll recover that much

1476
01:12:29,060 --> 01:12:30,220
The helicopter...

1477
01:12:30,220 --> 01:12:32,060
It's backup!

1478
01:12:32,060 --> 01:12:34,860
Go away!

1479
01:12:34,860 --> 01:12:37,680
How many shots does it take to bring down a helicopter?

1480
01:12:37,680 --> 01:12:41,200
And this one's a big one too

1481
01:12:41,200 --> 01:12:43,140
No no no, this is impossible

1482
01:12:43,140 --> 01:12:45,540
We're gonna die!

1483
01:12:45,540 --> 01:12:47,540
What even is that thing?

1484
01:12:47,540 --> 01:12:56,530
Why do they roll out the red carpet every time we try something?

1485
01:12:56,530 --> 01:12:58,530
It was going so well though

1486
01:12:58,530 --> 01:13:02,170
Whoa!

1487
01:13:02,170 --> 01:13:05,470
It's still here, right? Still here, still here — yeah it's totally still here, like...

1488
01:13:05,470 --> 01:13:08,970
It's circling around. Why is it hanging around here?

1489
01:13:08,970 --> 01:13:10,880
This one's patrolling too

1490
01:13:10,880 --> 01:13:14,270
Hey! Go home! Go home!

1491
01:13:15,370 --> 01:13:18,110
Polka's inventory is empty, okay?

1492
01:13:18,110 --> 01:13:20,810
I'm not carrying anything, no guns or anything

1493
01:13:20,810 --> 01:13:21,670
Don't look at me

1494
01:13:21,670 --> 01:13:24,210
How would it even know I have guns in my inventory?

1495
01:13:24,210 --> 01:13:26,150
That doesn't make sense

1496
01:13:26,150 --> 01:13:28,450
It's circling around though!

1497
01:13:28,450 --> 01:13:30,690
Hey...

1498
01:13:30,690 --> 01:13:33,850
Well, we've been spotted now, so whatever...

1499
01:13:33,850 --> 01:13:36,130
Four shots to take it down, Akai-san

1500
01:13:36,130 --> 01:13:37,570
That's about Akai-san, by the way

1501
01:13:37,570 --> 01:13:38,630
Four shots is enough?

1502
01:13:38,630 --> 01:13:39,470
Four shots and then...

1503
01:13:39,470 --> 01:13:44,690
Oh wait wait wait, it suddenly changed direction!

1504
01:13:44,690 --> 01:13:47,770
Hey, could you please stop with the anti-air?

1505
01:13:47,770 --> 01:13:52,190
Seriously, this is bad — we're getting hit from both land and air

1506
01:13:52,190 --> 01:13:54,490
Oh, it moved away! The helicopter moved away!

1507
01:13:54,490 --> 01:13:55,130
Did it leave?

1508
01:13:55,130 --> 01:13:56,890
I want to wait just a little longer

1509
01:13:56,890 --> 01:13:58,790
Goodbye!

1510
01:13:58,790 --> 01:14:00,690
Go home!

1511
01:14:00,690 --> 01:14:03,090
Is it... going home?

1512
01:14:03,090 --> 01:14:04,690
Yeah, it's leaving, it's really leaving right now

1513
01:14:04,690 --> 01:14:05,390
It's gone, it's gone!

1514
01:14:05,390 --> 01:14:07,090
And now it's gonna be night

1515
01:14:07,090 --> 01:14:11,070
Things were going so well too

1516
01:14:12,870 --> 01:14:14,030
Goodbye!

1517
01:14:14,030 --> 01:14:17,380
Goodbye, and please never come back~!

1518
01:14:17,380 --> 01:14:21,110
What was that all about?!

1519
01:14:21,110 --> 01:14:24,230
Things were going so well

1520
01:14:24,230 --> 01:14:28,810
Those guys run a fever when they catch a cold, you know

1521
01:14:28,810 --> 01:14:29,230
I had no idea.

1522
01:14:29,230 --> 01:14:35,060
Oh, it's still stuck.

1523
01:14:35,060 --> 01:14:36,620
It's still stuck.

1524
01:14:36,620 --> 01:14:42,290
Stay stuck! Please!

1525
01:14:42,290 --> 01:14:43,970
Oh, nice~

1526
01:14:45,730 --> 01:14:47,730
I can hear it hitting.

1527
01:14:47,730 --> 01:14:50,530
Is it a night battle, Luna? Did you open the rock already?

1528
01:14:50,530 --> 01:14:52,530
No, it should get dark soon.

1529
01:14:52,530 --> 01:14:55,050
Really?

1530
01:14:55,050 --> 01:14:56,850
Oh! Did we get it?

1531
01:14:56,850 --> 01:14:58,650
Huh?

1532
01:14:58,650 --> 01:15:00,650
We did it, Luna! It's working!

1533
01:15:00,650 --> 01:15:01,450
Did we get it?

1534
01:15:01,450 --> 01:15:02,450
It's over! It's done!

1535
01:15:02,450 --> 01:15:03,450
It's finished!

1536
01:15:03,450 --> 01:15:06,450
The battle is over!

1537
01:15:06,450 --> 01:15:08,050
The battle is over!

1538
01:15:08,050 --> 01:15:11,650
The battle is over!

1539
01:15:11,650 --> 01:15:13,650
While Polka was struggling,

1540
01:15:13,650 --> 01:15:15,250
Kanatan landed all the hits.

1541
01:15:15,250 --> 01:15:15,750
Hiyah!

1542
01:15:15,750 --> 01:15:18,250
Luna was shooting too.

1543
01:15:18,250 --> 01:15:20,350
Luna was shooting too!

1544
01:15:20,350 --> 01:15:23,650
Oh, it's burning, it's burning!

1545
01:15:23,650 --> 01:15:25,250
Woooah!

1546
01:15:25,250 --> 01:15:27,250
Wow, getting stuck is rough.

1547
01:15:27,250 --> 01:15:29,150
We've lost to getting stuck like three times ourselves.

1548
01:15:29,150 --> 01:15:30,050
About three times.

1549
01:15:30,050 --> 01:15:32,850
This spot keeps getting you stuck.

1550
01:15:32,850 --> 01:15:35,250
It's burning nicely.

1551
01:15:35,250 --> 01:15:37,250
It's super hot, okay?

1552
01:15:37,250 --> 01:15:40,050
Once this fire goes out,

1553
01:15:40,050 --> 01:15:42,350
three crates will appear and we collect them.

1554
01:15:42,350 --> 01:15:45,350
Right, you can't get close while it's still on fire.

1555
01:15:45,350 --> 01:15:49,170
Hot hot hot hot hot hot!

1556
01:15:49,170 --> 01:15:52,770
Yep, it burned — yesterday my belly got burned too.

1557
01:15:52,770 --> 01:15:53,970
Like,

1558
01:15:53,970 --> 01:15:56,600
you just get drawn in.

1559
01:15:56,600 --> 01:15:57,600
We did it! You just get drawn in.

1560
01:15:57,600 --> 01:16:00,200
Congratulations!

1561
01:16:00,200 --> 01:16:01,400
We did it!

1562
01:16:01,400 --> 01:16:05,400
Victory is ours! And it feels great seeing it show up on the map too.

1563
01:16:05,400 --> 01:16:08,400
Oh, you're right.

1564
01:16:08,400 --> 01:16:09,800
For everyone to see —

1565
01:16:10,400 --> 01:16:15,300
"We did it!" Yeah, we did!

1566
01:16:15,300 --> 01:16:25,300
Woo, commemorative photo — oh, I forgot to bring a camera. Screenshot, screenshot! No camera though.

1567
01:16:26,580 --> 01:16:34,400
Yesterday's practice really paid off. It really did.

1568
01:16:34,400 --> 01:16:42,320
If we hadn't practiced yesterday, it would've been really tough to teach Polka everything.

1569
01:16:42,320 --> 01:16:46,920
For sure, we both would've been completely wrecked.

1570
01:16:46,920 --> 01:16:50,460
It was seriously rough.

1571
01:16:50,460 --> 01:16:58,520
So our battle is finally over too. Yeah, finally.

1572
01:16:58,520 --> 01:17:02,240
Now there's nothing left to regret...

1573
01:17:02,600 --> 01:17:04,100
Right?

1574
01:17:04,100 --> 01:17:06,000
Hmm... yeah, I guess not.

1575
01:17:06,000 --> 01:17:07,080
Is there still something?

1576
01:17:07,080 --> 01:17:11,260
I feel like we really gave it our all.

1577
01:17:11,260 --> 01:17:13,800
We really did.

1578
01:17:13,800 --> 01:17:16,360
We did it!

1579
01:17:16,360 --> 01:17:18,200
What about the heli? The heli is insane.

1580
01:17:18,200 --> 01:17:19,140
Insane, the heli is insane.

1581
01:17:19,140 --> 01:17:20,960
The heli sounds terrifying.

1582
01:17:20,960 --> 01:17:23,380
The heli...

1583
01:17:23,380 --> 01:17:25,720
But if you hit it enough it goes down, right? That's impressive.

1584
01:17:25,720 --> 01:17:26,560
And then—

1585
01:17:26,560 --> 01:17:29,400
if it goes down, the missiles hit and you die.

1586
01:17:29,400 --> 01:17:30,940
Yeah, exactly.

1587
01:17:30,940 --> 01:17:35,020
There's no dodging a heli with just a crab cannon.

1588
01:17:35,020 --> 01:17:36,540
The crab cannon wouldn't cut it, right?

1589
01:17:36,540 --> 01:17:39,780
The crab cannon is the least of your worries with a heli.

1590
01:17:39,780 --> 01:17:45,560
I don't even know how you're supposed to deal with the heli.

1591
01:17:45,560 --> 01:17:47,400
Hmm...

1592
01:17:47,400 --> 01:17:49,000
Hmm...

1593
01:17:49,000 --> 01:17:50,400
Homing missiles.

1594
01:17:50,400 --> 01:17:51,900
I wonder...

1595
01:17:51,900 --> 01:17:53,400
Oh, there are homing ones?

1596
01:17:53,400 --> 01:17:55,420
Oh right, we had homing missiles at the base.

1597
01:17:55,420 --> 01:17:57,780
Yeah, yeah we did.

1598
01:17:57,780 --> 01:17:59,040
I see.

1599
01:17:59,660 --> 01:18:02,500
The heli is still a no-go.

1600
01:18:02,500 --> 01:18:04,420
Yeah, the heli is still out of the question.

1601
01:18:04,420 --> 01:18:06,220
A mini heli takes 4 shots

1602
01:18:06,220 --> 01:18:08,220
That last one was a big one

1603
01:18:08,220 --> 01:18:14,260
Even 4 shots is tough when it's hovering around up there

1604
01:18:14,260 --> 01:18:24,020
There's a crate over there

1605
01:18:24,020 --> 01:18:32,040
There it is, there it is! I can see the crate and I wanna go touch it, but it's still hot — I just wanna go!

1606
01:18:32,040 --> 01:18:39,360
Can't resist, right? Yeah, I get it. We just can't help wanting to open crates when we see them. Especially at the end. Yeah.

1607
01:18:39,360 --> 01:18:46,580
Like in real life, when you see screws you just wanna scrap them. Just the super ball? Wait, why?

1608
01:18:46,580 --> 01:18:52,070
Why? It's a super ball.

1609
01:18:53,550 --> 01:18:57,470
It's on fire

1610
01:18:57,470 --> 01:19:00,650
Hope something good comes out of this

1611
01:19:00,650 --> 01:19:03,010
What do you want from it?

1612
01:19:03,010 --> 01:19:03,750
The fire is...

1613
01:19:03,750 --> 01:19:06,550
dying down

1614
01:19:06,550 --> 01:19:08,850
Come on, cool down faster

1615
01:19:08,850 --> 01:19:14,590
Still burning strong

1616
01:19:14,590 --> 01:19:16,130
Still going strong

1617
01:19:16,130 --> 01:19:21,160
Still, still, still

1618
01:19:21,160 --> 01:19:22,260
Guess we gotta cool it down

1619
01:19:22,260 --> 01:19:23,220
Should we dump water on it?

1620
01:19:23,220 --> 01:19:25,200
If we pour water on it we'll have to wait for it to cool

1621
01:19:25,200 --> 01:19:27,730
Oh, the fire's going out

1622
01:19:27,730 --> 01:19:28,760
It's going out?

1623
01:19:28,760 --> 01:19:33,450
I wonder what's inside~

1624
01:19:33,450 --> 01:19:35,550
I mean, Kanata, that...

1625
01:19:35,550 --> 01:19:39,170
Hey, I want the dream aim assist thing to drop too

1626
01:19:39,170 --> 01:19:40,530
Here we go!

1627
01:19:40,530 --> 01:19:42,910
It's still pretty hot but...

1628
01:19:42,910 --> 01:19:44,330
Oh, it's fine, it's fine

1629
01:19:44,330 --> 01:19:45,230
We're good already?

1630
01:19:45,230 --> 01:19:46,410
Okay, let's check the first one

1631
01:19:46,410 --> 01:19:47,230
Open it~

1632
01:19:47,230 --> 01:19:48,090
Here we go!

1633
01:19:48,090 --> 01:19:49,810
Here we go!

1634
01:19:49,810 --> 01:19:51,550
There's a Beancan grenade but...

1635
01:19:51,550 --> 01:19:58,250
Second one!

1636
01:19:58,250 --> 01:19:59,750
What's in the second one?

1637
01:19:59,750 --> 01:20:02,550
This one lying on its side

1638
01:20:02,550 --> 01:20:04,050
Okay

1639
01:20:04,050 --> 01:20:05,650
Oh! What's this?!

1640
01:20:05,650 --> 01:20:09,380
Let's go! Kanata!

1641
01:20:09,180 --> 01:20:11,180
No way!

1642
01:20:11,180 --> 01:20:12,480
First time getting this!

1643
01:20:13,180 --> 01:20:15,180
What the heck is this?!

1644
01:20:15,180 --> 01:20:17,180
Try shooting it!

1645
01:20:17,180 --> 01:20:19,180
Of all places, it dropped here!

1646
01:20:19,180 --> 01:20:21,180
Let's gooo!

1647
01:20:21,180 --> 01:20:27,380
All that hard work paid off!

1648
01:20:27,180 --> 01:20:29,180
Let's open the other one too

1649
01:20:29,180 --> 01:20:30,540
Yesss!

1650
01:20:30,540 --> 01:20:32,300
Yay!

1651
01:20:32,300 --> 01:20:34,900
One more — where is it, where — ah, this one! Ready, toss!

1652
01:20:34,900 --> 01:20:35,720
Yeah!

1653
