1673
01:21:24,980 --> 01:21:26,460
Wait... oh...

1674
01:21:26,460 --> 01:21:28,880
So, where, where, where...

1675
01:21:28,880 --> 01:21:30,800
Over there, over there, over there!

1676
01:21:30,800 --> 01:21:31,400
Still can't break it...

1677
01:21:31,400 --> 01:21:32,400
Wait, still hot?

1678
01:21:32,400 --> 01:21:34,200
Over there, over there, over there...

1679
01:21:34,200 --> 01:21:37,600
Over there, over there, over there, over there...

1680
01:21:37,600 --> 01:21:39,560
It's still hot — the Beancan is still burning!

1681
01:21:39,560 --> 01:21:41,360


1682
01:21:41,360 --> 01:21:43,360
Polka was literally on fire there!

1683
01:21:43,360 --> 01:21:45,360


1684
01:21:45,360 --> 01:21:47,360


1685
01:21:47,360 --> 01:21:49,160
I'm on fire, but—

1686
01:21:49,160 --> 01:21:50,960
Still—

1687
01:21:50,960 --> 01:21:52,760
Oh!

1688
01:21:52,760 --> 01:21:54,760
I hear animal sounds, Hime!

1689
01:21:54,760 --> 01:21:56,560
It's here, it's here!

1690
01:21:56,560 --> 01:21:58,360
It's right here!

1691
01:21:58,360 --> 01:22:01,160
The Bradley! Shoot it, shoot it, shoot it!

1692
01:22:01,160 --> 01:22:03,060
Yeah!

1693
01:22:03,060 --> 01:22:05,060
This thing is heavy.

1694
01:22:05,060 --> 01:22:06,860
The bullets are insane!

1695
01:22:06,860 --> 01:22:08,860
The heli too— wait, is the heli far?

1696
01:22:08,860 --> 01:22:09,920
Is the heli far?

1697
01:22:09,920 --> 01:22:11,810
Try defending with this thing!

1698
01:22:11,810 --> 01:22:14,720
Wait, it holds 100 rounds? Whoa— okay!

1699
01:22:14,720 --> 01:22:17,520
Hey, can we shoot that heli?

1700
01:22:17,520 --> 01:22:20,120
Suddenly so bold?

1701
01:22:20,120 --> 01:22:21,920
I mean, come on—

1702
01:22:21,920 --> 01:22:24,720
It's pretty far away though, isn't it?

1703
01:22:24,720 --> 01:22:26,590
Oh!

1704
01:22:26,590 --> 01:22:29,520
This makes me feel so powerful!

1705
01:22:29,520 --> 01:22:31,460
It's like a machine gun!

1706
01:22:31,460 --> 01:22:33,320
Oh! Oh!

1707
01:22:33,320 --> 01:22:35,920
But it pulls way up when I shoot.

1708
01:22:35,920 --> 01:22:37,920
Yeah, the recoil is intense.

1709
01:22:37,920 --> 01:22:40,720
Is there something to reduce the recoil?

1710
01:22:40,720 --> 01:22:44,520
Like, can you customize it somehow?

1711
01:22:44,520 --> 01:22:47,120
Incredible.

1712
01:22:47,120 --> 01:22:50,120
M249.

1713
01:22:50,120 --> 01:22:52,920
The M249 is no joke.

1714
01:22:52,920 --> 01:22:55,920
Whoa, it was shooting at us from all the way over there?

1715
01:22:55,920 --> 01:22:58,720
That's awful. Unforgivable.

1716
01:22:58,720 --> 01:23:00,720
Incredible.

1717
01:23:03,200 --> 01:23:05,200
I can't forgive that tank!

1718
01:23:05,200 --> 01:23:07,200
What if you crouch while shooting?

1719
01:23:07,200 --> 01:23:09,120
Does crouching make it easier to shoot?

1720
01:23:09,120 --> 01:23:11,000
Yeah, it might reduce the recoil a bit.

1721
01:23:11,000 --> 01:23:15,800
I can't believe we actually got one!

1722
01:23:15,800 --> 01:23:18,600
Well, Polka believed it would happen.

1723
01:23:18,600 --> 01:23:22,200
Polka believed.

1724
01:23:22,200 --> 01:23:27,200
If you're gonna fight a tank, go all in!

1725
01:23:38,930 --> 01:23:40,910
Whoa! It's scrap metal!

1726
01:23:40,910 --> 01:23:42,710
Yay!

1727
01:23:42,710 --> 01:23:45,510
We did it!

1728
01:23:45,510 --> 01:23:47,310
Everything just dropped out of it!

1729
01:23:47,310 --> 01:23:51,110
Got the metal fragments too. Alright!

1730
01:23:51,110 --> 01:23:53,910
What?!

1731
01:23:53,910 --> 01:23:54,910
We won just like that!

1732
01:23:54,910 --> 01:23:56,710
That's amazing!

1733
01:23:56,710 --> 01:23:58,510
Let's go!

1734
01:23:58,510 --> 01:24:00,310
We did it!

1735
01:24:00,310 --> 01:24:02,110
We actually—!

1736
01:24:02,110 --> 01:24:04,110
We won!

1737
01:24:04,110 --> 01:24:04,910
Woo! Woo! Woohoo!

1738
01:24:04,910 --> 01:24:05,910
We won!

1739
01:24:06,510 --> 01:24:08,510
Yay, yay!

1740
01:24:08,510 --> 01:24:10,510
We won!

1741
01:24:10,510 --> 01:24:12,510
HoloLuna wins!

1742
01:24:12,510 --> 01:24:14,510
Victory!

1743
01:24:14,510 --> 01:24:16,510
Amazing!

1744
01:24:16,510 --> 01:24:18,510
That's the M249 for you.

1745
01:24:18,510 --> 01:24:20,510
You jerk.

1746
01:24:20,510 --> 01:24:22,510
Who knew it'd show up on the last day!

1747
01:24:22,510 --> 01:24:26,510
We were a bit of a slow start, huh.

1748
01:24:26,510 --> 01:24:28,510
That's true.

1749
01:24:28,510 --> 01:24:30,510
We were slow starters, but—

1750
01:24:30,510 --> 01:24:33,770
We won't get to see this thing in action again.

1751
01:24:37,130 --> 01:24:40,630
Somehow, in the night session, somehow—

1752
01:24:40,630 --> 01:24:43,570
Are we doing something in the night session?

1753
01:24:43,570 --> 01:24:45,770
No, not really anything planned.

1754
01:24:45,770 --> 01:24:49,830
But hey, we got to fight the tank!

1755
01:24:49,830 --> 01:24:52,690
That's amazing — we really made the most of it!

1756
01:24:52,690 --> 01:24:55,920
We did it!

1757
01:24:55,920 --> 01:24:59,500
So we managed to do a lot of things we couldn't do last time, right?

1758
01:24:59,500 --> 01:25:01,150
Polka got to do so much. Polka: Yeah, I really did!

1759
01:25:01,150 --> 01:25:04,050
It was my first time fighting a tank!

1760
01:25:04,890 --> 01:25:05,890
Right?!

1761
01:25:05,890 --> 01:25:09,190
Doing laps like this is terrifying — it takes years off your life

1762
01:25:09,190 --> 01:25:10,690
It really does

1763
01:25:10,690 --> 01:25:12,690
My lifespan is just draining away

1764
01:25:12,690 --> 01:25:13,990
doing this kind of thing

1765
01:25:13,990 --> 01:25:16,790
It looks easy but it's actually brutal

1766
01:25:16,790 --> 01:25:22,240
Well, the tank was basically stuck the whole time

1767
01:25:22,240 --> 01:25:25,040
so it felt a little easier than I expected

1768
01:25:25,040 --> 01:25:28,040
That's part of it — it wasn't moving

1769
01:25:28,040 --> 01:25:29,870
Hello, helicopter

1770
01:25:29,870 --> 01:25:31,840
Is the heli coming again?

1771
01:25:31,840 --> 01:25:33,640
A little heli

1772
01:25:33,940 --> 01:25:35,220
Oh wait, it's not coming

1773
01:25:35,220 --> 01:25:38,890
Nope, not coming

1774
01:25:38,890 --> 01:25:41,910
Since it's just us here, the heli comes for us constantly

1775
01:25:41,910 --> 01:25:44,850
Targeting us specifically

1776
01:25:44,850 --> 01:25:47,270
Have we done something wrong?

1777
01:25:47,270 --> 01:25:49,030
We have

1778
01:25:49,030 --> 01:25:51,930
We did — the tank

1779
01:25:51,930 --> 01:25:54,170
We did — we took out the tank

1780
01:25:54,170 --> 01:25:58,060
But hey, Kanatan — Kanatan still can't log in today, right?

1781
01:25:58,060 --> 01:25:59,730
I want to report back to her though

1782
01:26:00,590 --> 01:26:01,590
Yeah, we should

1783
01:26:01,590 --> 01:26:03,590
Yeah, it was Kanata's dream after all

1784
01:26:03,590 --> 01:26:07,890
And of all things, we got an M249

1785
01:26:07,890 --> 01:26:12,390
She said she wanted an M249 from the Golden Egg event

1786
01:26:12,390 --> 01:26:16,690
And we got one from the tank

1787
01:26:16,690 --> 01:26:18,850
Close enough!

1788
01:26:18,850 --> 01:26:19,850


1789
01:26:19,850 --> 01:26:25,200
Who's that over there?

1790
01:26:25,200 --> 01:26:26,500
Should we head back?

1791
01:26:26,500 --> 01:26:27,500
Should we head back?

1792
01:26:27,500 --> 01:26:28,800
They said it looks like her

1793
01:26:28,800 --> 01:26:30,800
They said it looks like her — that's actually a compliment

1794
01:26:30,800 --> 01:26:31,800
Looks like her

1795
01:26:31,800 --> 01:26:35,470
No missile launcher though

1796
01:26:35,470 --> 01:26:40,200
Here it comes again

1797
01:26:40,200 --> 01:26:44,480
Egg Hunt

1798
01:26:44,480 --> 01:26:45,480
It's Egg Hunt time!

1799
01:26:45,480 --> 01:26:47,480
Fun fun Egg Hunt~

1800
01:26:47,480 --> 01:26:50,280
We don't have time for that right now

1801
01:26:50,280 --> 01:26:53,080
Seriously

1802
01:26:53,080 --> 01:26:55,080
Right now it's all fun and games

1803
01:26:55,080 --> 01:26:56,880
The tank battle is over

1804
01:26:56,880 --> 01:27:00,460
and now we're just winding down

1805
01:27:00,460 --> 01:27:02,420
I'm so glad we pulled it off

1806
01:27:02,420 --> 01:27:04,220
Me too, seriously

1807
01:27:04,220 --> 01:27:06,220
The shadow was brutal

1808
01:27:06,220 --> 01:27:10,020
The zombie attack was insane

1809
01:27:10,020 --> 01:27:12,020
It really was a zombie attack

1810
01:27:12,020 --> 01:27:17,400
You okay? Looks like the shadow almost got you

1811
01:27:17,400 --> 01:27:19,400
Running straight at the shadow

1812
01:27:19,400 --> 01:27:21,350
Nice, nice!

1813
01:27:21,350 --> 01:27:23,960
Yay!

1814
01:27:23,960 --> 01:27:25,980
Yay!

1815
01:27:26,980 --> 01:27:28,830
The life-saving door slam

1816
01:27:28,830 --> 01:27:30,780
The life-saving door slam

1817
01:27:30,780 --> 01:27:32,580
Right?

1818
01:27:32,580 --> 01:27:33,580
Polka was just—

1819
01:27:33,580 --> 01:27:34,380
Yeah yeah

1820
01:27:34,380 --> 01:27:35,200
Slam!

1821
01:27:35,200 --> 01:27:37,180
That was a nice move

1822
01:27:37,180 --> 01:27:44,200
We both kind of won through bugs though

1823
01:27:44,200 --> 01:27:47,200
The tank was stuck, so we got a free win too

1824
01:27:47,200 --> 01:27:48,200
That's true

1825
01:27:48,200 --> 01:27:49,180
Right?

1826
01:27:49,180 --> 01:27:51,000
50-50

1827
01:27:51,000 --> 01:27:52,800
We're even

1828
01:27:52,800 --> 01:27:53,800
Exactly

1829
01:27:53,800 --> 01:27:55,600
Gonna crash into it

1830
01:27:55,600 --> 01:27:57,200
Left

1831
01:27:57,200 --> 01:27:59,200
OK

1832
01:27:59,200 --> 01:28:02,520
We took down the elite

1833
01:28:02,520 --> 01:28:04,520
I'm fully satisfied now

1834
01:28:04,520 --> 01:28:06,320
Are we fighting?

1835
01:28:06,320 --> 01:28:08,320
Are we fighting?

1836
01:28:08,320 --> 01:28:11,290
We've done everything we set out to do

1837
01:28:11,290 --> 01:28:13,090
We've done everything we set out to do

1838
01:28:13,090 --> 01:28:14,890
Last one

1839
01:28:14,890 --> 01:28:18,490
There's an elite

1840
01:28:18,490 --> 01:28:20,490
An elite showed up

1841
01:28:20,490 --> 01:28:22,490
Trainyard.

1842
01:28:22,490 --> 01:28:26,290
Oh, it's not the ferry. The tank, the tank!

1843
01:28:26,290 --> 01:28:28,090
Right, right, right!

1844
01:28:28,090 --> 01:28:30,890
I can already see the base.

1845
01:28:30,890 --> 01:28:32,890
It's so close, so close!

1846
01:28:32,890 --> 01:28:33,890
Turn right!

1847
01:28:33,890 --> 01:28:35,570
What happened to the heli?!

1848
01:28:35,570 --> 01:28:36,490
What happened to the heli?!

1849
01:29:05,800 --> 01:29:06,800
No way!

1850
01:29:06,600 --> 01:29:07,100
Ah!

1851
01:29:07,100 --> 01:29:10,420
Help me!

1852
01:29:10,420 --> 01:29:13,560
Hey!

1853
01:29:13,560 --> 01:29:14,940
Alright! That's fine!

1854
01:29:14,940 --> 01:29:17,640
What am I supposed to do if my M249 burns up?!

1855
01:29:17,640 --> 01:29:19,360
Oh, it really did!

1856
01:29:19,360 --> 01:29:28,020
Dying to an explosion is the worst!

1857
01:29:28,020 --> 01:29:32,440
I didn't want to die to an explosion!

1858
01:29:32,440 --> 01:29:33,820
I'm going home!

1859
01:29:35,360 --> 01:29:37,360
That thing is the absolute worst!

1860
01:29:37,360 --> 01:29:39,360
Ahaha! Right?!

1861
01:29:39,360 --> 01:29:41,360
Unforgivable!

1862
01:29:41,360 --> 01:29:45,360
Ugh! There were moments I thought I kinda liked the heli, but...

1863
01:29:45,360 --> 01:29:48,360
Hey hey! The car!

1864
01:29:48,360 --> 01:29:51,360
Get in the back! Luna!

1865
01:29:51,360 --> 01:29:52,360
The heli, is the heli okay?

1866
01:29:52,360 --> 01:29:53,360
I don't know!

1867
01:29:53,360 --> 01:29:54,360
Is anyone there?

1868
01:29:54,360 --> 01:29:55,360
Get in the back!

1869
01:29:55,360 --> 01:29:56,360
Did you get in? Got in, got in!

1870
01:29:56,360 --> 01:29:59,360
We need to show them we're harmless.

1871
01:30:01,090 --> 01:30:03,360
Dammit!

1872
01:30:06,820 --> 01:30:08,660
Hey, the camper van again...

1873
01:30:08,450 --> 01:30:10,260
Something broke.

1874
01:30:10,260 --> 01:30:12,250
Did everything break?

1875
01:30:12,250 --> 01:30:14,050
It just keeps breaking, doesn't it.

1876
01:30:14,050 --> 01:30:17,850
Whoa, it's a sea of fire.

1877
01:30:17,850 --> 01:30:19,650
Oh, something...

1878
01:30:19,650 --> 01:30:21,250
is coming.

1879
01:30:21,250 --> 01:30:23,050
Someone...

1880
01:30:23,050 --> 01:30:24,650
Huh?

1881
01:30:24,650 --> 01:30:26,590
There was someone just now, right?

1882
01:30:26,590 --> 01:30:28,450
Hello!

1883
01:30:28,450 --> 01:30:30,450
Are you okay?

1884
01:30:30,450 --> 01:30:32,250
Our corpses are...

1885
01:30:32,250 --> 01:30:34,250
Oh no, thank you!

1886
01:30:34,250 --> 01:30:36,050
Did the bear take care of it?

1887
01:30:36,050 --> 01:30:37,850
Oh no, oh no, oh no...

1888
01:30:37,850 --> 01:30:39,650
The bear died on its own.

1889
01:30:39,650 --> 01:30:41,650
The bear just died on its own. Okay.

1890
01:30:41,650 --> 01:30:43,450
Probably...

1891
01:30:43,450 --> 01:30:45,450
it came to eat this person

1892
01:30:45,450 --> 01:30:47,250
and got burned by the flames.

1893
01:30:47,250 --> 01:30:51,050
Thank you.

1894
01:30:51,050 --> 01:30:53,050
We're fine, but the camper van broke.

1895
01:30:53,050 --> 01:30:54,830
Oh, don't worry about it!

1896
01:30:54,830 --> 01:30:56,650
Ah, that's rough.

1897
01:30:56,650 --> 01:30:58,450
I see.

1898
01:30:58,450 --> 01:31:00,450
I was just logging in and

1899
01:31:00,450 --> 01:31:03,070
I was lying down and heard this huge noise...

1900
01:31:03,070 --> 01:31:06,910
Oh wait, this is Polka's stuff.

1901
01:31:06,910 --> 01:31:09,670
Sorry for scaring you, it's okay!

1902
01:31:09,670 --> 01:31:14,270
It's totally fine, all good, no worries at all!

1903
01:31:14,270 --> 01:31:16,550
Where's Unata's body? Oh, is this it?

1904
01:31:16,550 --> 01:31:20,350
There are 3 bodies lying around, so it should be fine, right?

1905
01:31:20,350 --> 01:31:22,850
The bodies look okay for now.

1906
01:31:26,190 --> 01:31:29,570
Ugh, that scared me!

1907
01:31:29,570 --> 01:31:33,180
What was that thing?!

1908
01:31:33,180 --> 01:31:35,070
Hime!!

1909
01:31:35,070 --> 01:31:38,320
We died way too many times.

1910
01:31:49,240 --> 01:31:51,420
And not even from the tank...

1911
01:31:51,420 --> 01:31:56,260
Was it a mama bear and a cub?

1912
01:31:56,260 --> 01:31:58,100
Come on, seriously...

1913
01:32:00,070 --> 01:32:04,070
This time we took damage from something other than the tank.

1914
01:32:04,070 --> 01:32:05,070
We're okay!

1915
01:32:05,070 --> 01:32:06,070
We're fine!

1916
01:32:06,070 --> 01:32:12,840
A bonus bear showed up, but we're okay!

1917
01:32:12,840 --> 01:32:14,840
Come on~

1918
01:32:14,840 --> 01:32:17,840
Sorry, I panicked and started shooting.

1919
01:32:17,840 --> 01:32:19,840
Yeah...

1920
01:32:19,840 --> 01:32:21,640
Thank you.

1921
01:32:21,640 --> 01:32:23,640
The patrol's back! The patrol's here!

1922
01:32:23,640 --> 01:32:27,640
Give back the M249!

1923
01:32:30,420 --> 01:32:32,100
Wait up!

1924
01:32:31,900 --> 01:32:34,050
Oh no, I'm being targeted, what do I do?

1925
01:32:34,440 --> 01:32:35,120
Run!

1926
01:32:35,120 --> 01:32:37,760
There are way too many bodies rolling around in front of our junior's house!

1927
01:32:37,760 --> 01:32:38,760
Right?!

1928
01:32:38,760 --> 01:32:42,460
What if it hits Niko-tan's house?!

1929
01:32:42,460 --> 01:32:44,960
That would be such an accident!

1930
01:32:44,960 --> 01:32:48,380
Wait, a bear?! Are you kidding me?!

1931
01:32:48,380 --> 01:32:50,520
I didn't expect two bears to show up!

1932
01:32:50,520 --> 01:32:54,360
Did this turn into a corpse? A dead body?

1933
01:32:54,360 --> 01:32:54,860
This one?

1934
01:32:54,860 --> 01:32:56,680
Wait, which one is Una-tan?

1935
01:32:56,680 --> 01:32:58,120
That one, the blue one!

1936
01:32:58,120 --> 01:32:59,640
Oh, this one, this one!

1937
01:32:59,440 --> 01:33:01,960
Ugh, are you kidding me?!

1938
01:33:01,960 --> 01:33:04,880
Seriously, that guy...

1939
01:33:04,880 --> 01:33:05,600
I'm tearing up.

1940
01:33:05,600 --> 01:33:08,360
That guy's totally a stalker, right?

1941
01:33:08,360 --> 01:33:09,280
What is his deal?

1942
01:33:09,280 --> 01:33:13,200
He's way too obsessed with us.

1943
01:33:13,200 --> 01:33:15,040
This is Paw Patrol, right?

1944
01:33:15,040 --> 01:33:16,000
Yeah, which one?

1945
01:33:16,000 --> 01:33:18,060
Under Paw Patrol.

1946
01:33:18,060 --> 01:33:19,860
Oh, but there's nothing on it.

1947
01:33:19,860 --> 01:33:21,320
This one says "Himemori is here."

1948
01:33:21,320 --> 01:33:22,460
This is Paw Patrol.

1949
01:33:22,460 --> 01:33:25,980
There are seriously too many bodies lying around.

1950
01:33:25,980 --> 01:33:27,480
This is the worst.

1951
01:33:27,480 --> 01:33:29,780
The camper van got wrecked too.

1952
01:33:29,780 --> 01:33:31,680
Well, it's not completely destroyed.

1953
01:33:31,680 --> 01:33:34,540
It looks like we can repair it, more so than last time.

1954
01:33:34,540 --> 01:33:36,580
Oh, you're right.

1955
01:33:36,580 --> 01:33:39,460
Scary...

1956
01:33:39,460 --> 01:33:41,080
But still, you know?

1957
01:33:41,080 --> 01:33:45,420
Can we fix it?

1958
01:33:45,420 --> 01:33:47,220
A hammer...

1959
01:33:47,220 --> 01:33:48,920
Hmm...

1960
01:33:48,920 --> 01:33:56,000
The sounds around here are scary again.

1961
01:33:56,000 --> 01:33:57,280
Is the heli coming?

1962
01:33:57,280 --> 01:33:59,100
The heli's close!

1963
01:33:59,100 --> 01:34:01,220
It's just nearby, just nearby, just nearby!

1964
01:34:01,220 --> 01:34:03,160
Still scary though.

1965
01:34:03,160 --> 01:34:03,860
It's just nearby.

1966
01:34:03,860 --> 01:34:08,050
I don't even know anymore.

1967
01:34:08,050 --> 01:34:11,110
We've been attacked so much I can't tell what's going on.

1968
01:34:11,110 --> 01:34:13,490
What do those guys even want?

1969
01:34:13,490 --> 01:34:17,050
To kill us.

1970
01:34:17,050 --> 01:34:18,850
That's terrifying!

1971
01:34:18,850 --> 01:34:20,850
No wood, so we can't repair it.

1972
01:34:20,850 --> 01:34:26,450
We got spotted and they locked on to us.

1973
01:34:26,450 --> 01:34:35,310
We're close enough to just walk back, it's fine.

1974
01:34:35,310 --> 01:34:36,110
True.

1975
01:34:36,110 --> 01:34:38,710
We don't even need the car anymore, do we?

1976
01:34:38,710 --> 01:34:42,510
You worked so hard to build it though.

1977
01:34:43,510 --> 01:34:47,630
We lost two cars in just a few hours today.

1978
01:34:47,630 --> 01:34:53,380
We burned through them too fast.

1979
01:34:53,380 --> 01:34:56,270
They got wrecked so quickly.

1980
01:34:56,270 --> 01:35:01,610
Way too fast.

1981
01:35:01,610 --> 01:35:04,030
Alright, we're abandoning this one. Thanks for your service.

1982
01:35:04,030 --> 01:35:06,970
There's a pouch around here somewhere.

1983
01:35:10,090 --> 01:35:12,090
It's already buried in junk.

1984
01:35:12,090 --> 01:35:17,530
Let's just head home.

1985
01:35:17,530 --> 01:35:22,490
There's trash scattered everywhere.

1986
01:35:22,490 --> 01:35:25,250
Right in front of our junior's house too—

1987
01:35:25,250 --> 01:35:27,770
Shooting off guns—

1988
01:35:27,770 --> 01:35:29,770
Leaving trash behind—

1989
01:35:29,770 --> 01:35:31,770
Ugh, come on!

1990
01:35:31,770 --> 01:35:34,130
We were so close to making it.

1991
01:35:34,130 --> 01:35:37,770
Seriously, it was right around the corner.

1992
01:35:37,770 --> 01:35:40,210
Our place was getting bombed too.

1993
01:35:40,490 --> 01:35:44,290
Seriously, thank goodness! Niko-tan, thank goodness you're safe!

1994
01:35:44,290 --> 01:35:47,090
I need to bring Niko-tan some kind of apology gift.

1995
01:35:47,090 --> 01:35:49,090
She almost got caught in the crossfire.

1996
01:35:49,090 --> 01:35:50,090
Yeah, seriously.

1997
01:35:50,090 --> 01:35:54,090
Niko-tan's house was getting blown up left and right, it was bad.

1998
01:35:54,090 --> 01:35:55,890
It really was.

1999
01:35:55,890 --> 01:35:59,690
Thank goodness. I need to bring her an apology gift.

2000
01:35:59,690 --> 01:36:01,490
What should I bring?

2001
01:36:01,490 --> 01:36:02,490
Phew~

2002
01:36:02,490 --> 01:36:04,290
Good work, everyone!

2003
01:36:04,290 --> 01:36:05,290
Man...

2004
01:36:05,290 --> 01:36:08,640
Kanata-so, I brought you an M249!

2005
01:36:08,640 --> 01:36:11,690
You have an M249?

2006
01:36:11,690 --> 01:36:13,490
Kanata-so is so happy!

2007
01:36:13,490 --> 01:36:16,420
Yes! An M249!

2008
01:36:16,420 --> 01:36:20,130
Don't point that gun at me!

2009
01:36:20,130 --> 01:36:25,940
We got the thing that was meant for us!

2010
01:36:25,940 --> 01:36:29,690
After losing our lives so many times...

2011
01:36:29,690 --> 01:36:31,690
We died so many times today too.

2012
01:36:31,690 --> 01:36:33,270
It's ridiculous, right?

2013
01:36:33,270 --> 01:36:37,150
You said it would go smoothly, remember?

2014
01:36:37,150 --> 01:36:38,750
We died for nothing so many times.

2015
01:36:38,750 --> 01:36:42,490
Seriously! We died so much and it wasn't even from the tank!

2016
01:36:42,490 --> 01:36:47,210
We died more to non-tank stuff than the actual tank.

2017
01:36:47,210 --> 01:36:49,430
Haah...

2018
01:36:49,430 --> 01:36:51,810
What even was that~

2019
01:36:51,810 --> 01:36:53,490


2020
01:36:53,490 --> 01:36:54,310
We did it!

2021
01:36:54,310 --> 01:36:56,070
Well, I wouldn't say "we did it" exactly...

2022
01:36:56,070 --> 01:36:57,110
We did it though!

2023
01:36:57,110 --> 01:36:59,690
It was those guys who actually did it.

2024
01:36:59,690 --> 01:37:02,400
That's the worst.

2025
01:37:02,400 --> 01:37:05,340
Weirdos.

2026
01:37:05,340 --> 01:37:07,300


2027
01:37:07,300 --> 01:37:12,590
That was fun though.

2028
01:37:12,590 --> 01:37:13,550
It really was fun.

2029
01:37:13,550 --> 01:37:15,450
Can't believe that kind of thing happens.

2030
01:37:15,450 --> 01:37:18,750
When you're alive, I mean.

2031
01:37:18,750 --> 01:37:22,210
Makes you glad to be alive.

2032
01:37:22,210 --> 01:37:24,510
Even though we died, it worked out somehow.

2033
01:37:24,510 --> 01:37:25,750
Right, glad to be alive, but...

2034
01:37:25,750 --> 01:37:26,750
We did die though.

2035
01:37:26,750 --> 01:37:28,750
It's hard to put into words.

2036
01:37:28,750 --> 01:37:35,580
Like, it was a fun experience, but we died.

2037
01:37:35,580 --> 01:37:39,040
Alright.

2038
01:37:39,040 --> 01:37:41,970
This and this.

2039
01:37:41,970 --> 01:37:45,670
We grew a little more today!

2040
01:37:45,670 --> 01:37:47,450
We did it!

2041
01:37:47,450 --> 01:37:51,210
Our rocket launcher ammo went up a crazy amount.

2042
01:37:51,210 --> 01:37:53,930
Do we have more than when we came?

2043
01:37:53,930 --> 01:37:55,590
Maybe not quite that much?

2044
01:37:55,590 --> 01:37:56,630
Because we picked some up?

2045
01:37:56,630 --> 01:37:59,370
Yeah, we picked some up — grabbed like 6!

2046
01:37:59,370 --> 01:38:01,250
Oh, so we've got quite a bit then.

2047
01:38:01,250 --> 01:38:03,250
Incendiary missiles too.

2048
01:38:03,250 --> 01:38:05,710
So maybe tonight we can do something with these...

2049
01:38:05,710 --> 01:38:07,010
This thing...

2050
01:38:07,010 --> 01:38:10,090
What was it called — some kind of rocket, used at the tank...

2051
01:38:10,090 --> 01:38:12,970
Or wait, is it the one you use at the military base?

2052
01:38:12,970 --> 01:38:15,830
Oh, the one that fires missiles?

2053
01:38:15,830 --> 01:38:18,090
That's basically PVP stuff at this point.

2054
01:38:18,090 --> 01:38:19,410
We don't need these.

2055
01:38:19,410 --> 01:38:20,870
Can't use them.

2056
01:38:20,870 --> 01:38:23,870
We haven't even used those yet.

2057
01:38:23,870 --> 01:38:25,090
Yeah, we can't really use them.

2058
01:38:25,430 --> 01:38:30,590
Doesn't that have a pretty long cooldown too?

2059
01:38:30,590 --> 01:38:34,110
You'd have to capture the military base first.

2060
01:38:34,110 --> 01:38:37,340
Oh really?

2061
01:38:37,340 --> 01:38:40,060
There were people at the military base too, right?

2062
01:38:40,060 --> 01:38:43,380
You hack the missile computer there and...

2063
01:38:43,380 --> 01:38:47,320
I have no idea how missiles work.

2064
01:38:47,320 --> 01:38:49,000
There's no way I can fire these.

2065
01:38:49,000 --> 01:38:52,080
Maybe in PVP it'd be possible, but...

2066
01:38:52,080 --> 01:38:54,640
I'd never use all 12 of these.

2067
01:38:54,640 --> 01:38:57,860
These are MLRS rockets.

2068
01:38:57,860 --> 01:38:59,400
I'm not going to use these.

2069
01:38:59,400 --> 01:39:01,740
Yeah, I won't be using these.

2070
01:39:01,740 --> 01:39:03,580
The ones you fire from the military base, right.

2071
01:39:03,580 --> 01:39:04,500
Yeah, exactly.

2072
01:39:04,500 --> 01:39:07,600
We don't need these.

2073
01:39:07,600 --> 01:39:09,160
Yeah, don't need them.

2074
01:39:09,160 --> 01:39:10,940
It's hopeless.

2075
01:39:10,940 --> 01:39:16,960
If this were PVP, we'd be in a really strong position right now.

2076
01:39:16,960 --> 01:39:20,810
Holding all these weapons...

2077
01:39:20,810 --> 01:39:24,190
True, but I still don't really know how to use them.

2078
01:39:24,190 --> 01:39:26,470
My skills just aren't quite there yet.

2079
01:39:26,470 --> 01:39:32,170
The heli's back.

2080
01:39:32,170 --> 01:39:32,950
Ugh, not the heli again.

2081
01:39:32,950 --> 01:39:34,110
The heli—

2082
01:39:34,110 --> 01:39:37,010
They've already figured out where we are.

2083
01:39:37,010 --> 01:39:38,150
Obviously.

2084
01:39:38,150 --> 01:39:39,530
Let me try shooting at it.

2085
01:39:39,530 --> 01:39:43,490
Huh?

2086
01:39:43,490 --> 01:39:44,410
Hime!

2087
01:39:44,410 --> 01:39:45,670
Homing! Homing!

2088
01:39:45,670 --> 01:39:46,770
Homing! Homing!

2089
01:39:46,770 --> 01:39:49,570
How many times have those guys killed us now?

2090
01:39:49,570 --> 01:39:51,570
Homing missile! Where was it? The homing missile!

2091
01:39:51,570 --> 01:39:58,140
The homing missile should be over there.

2092
01:39:58,140 --> 01:40:00,970
Isn't it getting closer though?

2093
01:40:00,970 --> 01:40:03,770
We're totally being targeted.

2094
01:40:03,770 --> 01:40:06,570
The homing— where is it?

2095
01:40:06,570 --> 01:40:08,370
It's a homing missile!

2096
01:40:08,370 --> 01:40:09,170
It should be here somewhere.

2097
01:40:09,170 --> 01:40:12,970
What's this? Ammo? What do I load it into?

2098
01:40:12,970 --> 01:40:17,950
Is this the rocket launcher for it? The homing launcher?

2099
01:40:17,950 --> 01:40:22,870
What do you mean— what are you calling the rocket launcher?

2100
01:40:22,870 --> 01:40:29,050
A dedicated launcher? I think there was one— like a homing launcher?

2101
01:40:29,050 --> 01:40:32,390
Is there one? Yes, there is!

2102
01:40:32,390 --> 01:40:36,970
This house has everything. It's crazy— this, this, this!

2103
01:40:36,970 --> 01:40:39,950
If we fire near the house it'll get destroyed though.

2104
01:40:39,950 --> 01:40:42,470
We moved a bit away, so load it up for me.

2105
01:40:42,470 --> 01:40:44,510
There's only one, by the way. Oh wait, there's more?

2106
01:40:44,510 --> 01:40:47,110
Hold on, let me see if I can make another one.

2107
01:40:47,110 --> 01:40:49,030
Hurry, the heli—

2108
01:40:49,030 --> 01:40:50,450
The heli's gonna leave!

2109
01:40:50,450 --> 01:40:54,170
The heli leaving is actually a good thing— it's only targeting us.

2110
01:40:54,170 --> 01:40:58,290
Niko, let's try not to cause trouble for others.

2111
01:40:58,290 --> 01:41:00,150
Let's move a bit away.

2112
01:41:00,150 --> 01:41:01,210
If we're gonna shoot—

2113
01:41:01,210 --> 01:41:06,690
Wait, can you even craft a homing launcher?

2114
01:41:06,690 --> 01:41:08,310
Can you craft it?

2115
01:41:08,560 --> 01:41:10,550
If you research it—

2116
01:41:10,550 --> 01:41:12,550
We've been throwing money at everything right now.

2117
01:41:12,550 --> 01:41:14,430
We can research it!

2118
01:41:14,430 --> 01:41:16,150
Oh, we can research it!

2119
01:41:16,150 --> 01:41:20,950
Alright!

2120
01:41:20,950 --> 01:41:21,750
Let's make it!

2121
01:41:21,750 --> 01:41:22,750
That heli—

2122
01:41:22,750 --> 01:41:24,750
We're gonna show that helicopter what we're made of!

2123
01:41:24,750 --> 01:41:25,750
For real!

2124
01:41:25,750 --> 01:41:27,550
With the homing missile—

2125
01:41:27,550 --> 01:41:29,350
We'll track it down!

2126
01:41:29,350 --> 01:41:32,150
Let's bring two homing missiles.

2127
01:41:32,150 --> 01:41:34,950
Sure!

2128
01:41:34,950 --> 01:41:36,750
Let's do this!

2129
01:41:36,750 --> 01:41:37,750
And then—

2130
01:41:38,590 --> 01:41:42,390
Let's avenge all our past deaths!

2131
01:41:42,390 --> 01:41:47,190
Wait— it needs a CCTV camera?

2132
01:41:47,190 --> 01:41:49,120
It needs a CCTV camera!

2133
01:41:49,120 --> 01:41:50,990
Just one?

2134
01:41:50,990 --> 01:41:56,410
CCTV camera... just one.

2135
01:41:56,410 --> 01:41:58,410
I dropped it, I dropped it.

2136
01:41:58,410 --> 01:41:59,410
Oh wait, it needs pipes too.

2137
01:41:59,410 --> 01:42:01,260
Do we have pipes? Still?

2138
01:42:01,260 --> 01:42:03,210
We used all the pipes.

2139
01:42:03,210 --> 01:42:07,010
We're out!

2140
01:42:07,010 --> 01:42:09,810
There are 13 in the trash can.

2141
01:42:09,810 --> 01:42:12,610
Pick up the CCTV there.

2142
01:42:12,610 --> 01:42:15,390
There are 13 in the trash can.

2143
01:42:15,390 --> 01:42:17,010
What?

2144
01:42:17,010 --> 01:42:19,010
Right here, this, this, this!

2145
01:42:19,010 --> 01:42:21,010
At your feet.

2146
01:42:21,010 --> 01:42:25,810
At your feet— and there are 13 pipes in the trash can.

2147
01:42:25,810 --> 01:42:29,610
There are 13 pipes there!

2148
01:42:29,610 --> 01:42:32,320
Where's the heli?

2149
01:42:32,320 --> 01:42:34,210
With this—

2150
01:42:34,210 --> 01:42:37,010
Did the heli move away? Let's call it back!

2151
01:42:37,010 --> 01:42:38,740
Hey, heli!

2152
01:42:38,740 --> 01:42:40,430
Heliiii!

2153
01:42:40,430 --> 01:42:43,230
Heli? It'll come, right?

2154
01:42:43,230 --> 01:42:45,210
NPCs!

2155
01:42:45,210 --> 01:42:46,810
Let's go! Let's go!

2156
01:42:46,810 --> 01:42:48,610
The house will get destroyed.

2157
01:42:48,610 --> 01:42:53,210
We don't want the heli destroying the house.

2158
01:42:53,210 --> 01:42:55,010
Exactly.

2159
01:42:55,010 --> 01:42:57,810
I'll go deal with the NPCs.

2160
01:42:57,810 --> 01:42:59,610
With this—

2161
01:43:02,070 --> 01:43:05,270
Wait, CCTV — I can only make one CCTV.

2162
01:43:05,270 --> 01:43:09,340
Huh, uh, blah blah blah...

2163
01:43:09,340 --> 01:43:12,410
Did we get it?

2164
01:43:12,410 --> 01:43:18,120
Huh? The helicopter sound stopped.

2165
01:43:18,120 --> 01:43:18,820
That's the worst.

2166
01:43:18,820 --> 01:43:21,120


2167
01:43:21,120 --> 01:43:24,130


2168
01:43:24,130 --> 01:43:25,230
Dang!

2169
01:43:25,230 --> 01:43:26,330
This...

2170
01:43:26,330 --> 01:43:28,830
I thought we actually got it!

2171
01:43:28,830 --> 01:43:33,600
What happened?

2172
01:43:33,600 --> 01:43:35,400
Huh? I was messing around with the NPCs.

2173
01:43:36,000 --> 01:43:39,800
Polka's hopeless.

2174
01:43:39,800 --> 01:43:43,600
Did you get taken out? You okay?

2175
01:43:43,600 --> 01:43:45,600
Yeah, yeah, I got taken out. Just like that.

2176
01:43:45,600 --> 01:43:48,400
Polka keeps getting killed, huh.

2177
01:43:48,400 --> 01:43:49,400
Because I'm weak.

2178
01:43:49,400 --> 01:43:54,200
Why though?

2179
01:43:54,200 --> 01:43:56,200
Hey, the heli ran away!

2180
01:43:56,200 --> 01:43:58,000
Get over here!

2181
01:43:58,000 --> 01:44:03,700
No camera.

2182
01:44:05,710 --> 01:44:15,530
You need a camera? The CCTV camera — is it a physical item? I only had the one I gave you. How many did you need?

2183
01:44:15,530 --> 01:44:22,570
I need one to make a homing missile. Wasn't the one I gave you enough?

2184
01:44:22,570 --> 01:44:26,790
I can make one, but not two.

2185
01:44:26,790 --> 01:44:30,630
But we each have one now, so thanks!

2186
01:44:30,890 --> 01:44:33,690
I used one to research it, so I only have one.

2187
01:44:33,690 --> 01:44:34,690
Ah, I see.

2188
01:44:34,690 --> 01:44:36,490
I only have one.

2189
01:44:36,490 --> 01:44:38,290
Then let's fight with one.

2190
01:44:38,290 --> 01:44:41,090
Let's do it together then.

2191
01:44:41,090 --> 01:44:42,090
Yeah, let's.

2192
01:44:42,090 --> 01:44:43,890
Yeah.

2193
01:44:43,890 --> 01:44:46,690
Yeah.

2194
01:44:46,690 --> 01:44:49,490
There are still NPCs here.

2195
01:44:49,490 --> 01:44:51,490
Watch out for them.

2196
01:44:51,490 --> 01:44:54,660
Where are the NPCs?

2197
01:44:54,660 --> 01:44:56,460
Straight ahead.

2198
01:44:59,810 --> 01:45:01,170
I can't shoot yet.

2199
01:45:01,170 --> 01:45:03,110
Huh? Am I a genius?

2200
01:45:03,110 --> 01:45:09,490
There's just the one.

2201
01:45:09,490 --> 01:45:12,290
The homing missile.

2202
01:45:12,290 --> 01:45:17,540
But the heli went somewhere.

2203
01:45:17,540 --> 01:45:20,900
Let's just get ready for it.

2204
01:45:20,900 --> 01:45:23,200
Oh, if I can't shoot it, I'll use the M249.

2205
01:45:23,200 --> 01:45:24,700
Okay, okay, okay.

2206
01:45:24,700 --> 01:45:26,500
Here, Polka.

2207
01:45:26,500 --> 01:45:28,600
Polka's the one shooting?

2208
01:45:28,600 --> 01:45:30,400
Use the homing missile.

2209
01:45:30,400 --> 01:45:33,800
It didn't even hit at this close range...

2210
01:45:33,800 --> 01:45:35,280
Polka's shooting it.

2211
01:45:35,280 --> 01:45:39,140
It's homing, so it should track the target.

2212
01:45:39,140 --> 01:45:41,440
Really?

2213
01:45:41,440 --> 01:45:43,200
Otherwise they wouldn't call it homing.

2214
01:45:43,200 --> 01:45:47,100
Can I get some ammo?

2215
01:45:47,100 --> 01:45:52,440
Oh, I had ammo.

2216
01:45:52,440 --> 01:45:55,700
Not that way.

2217
01:45:55,700 --> 01:46:00,490
Is it coming? Did it come?

2218
01:46:00,490 --> 01:46:02,490
Right in its pretty face!

2219
01:46:02,490 --> 01:46:06,200
This is the M249.

2220
01:46:06,200 --> 01:46:08,500
Whoa, this thing is insane!

2221
01:46:08,500 --> 01:46:10,920
First I want to get eyes on it.

2222
01:46:10,920 --> 01:46:17,920
Let's move away from the house.

2223
01:46:17,920 --> 01:46:21,000
So Niko doesn't get caught in the crossfire.

2224
01:46:21,000 --> 01:46:23,140
Where is it?

2225
01:46:23,140 --> 01:46:24,360
There's a horse over there.

2226
01:46:24,360 --> 01:46:26,330
Where?

2227
01:46:26,330 --> 01:46:29,010
Where is it?

2228
01:46:29,010 --> 01:46:30,010
Why is it that at times like this—

2229
01:46:30,010 --> 01:46:33,010
Ah! There it is! I see it, but— it's right in the snow... it's far! Is it far?

2230
01:46:33,010 --> 01:46:35,110
It's pretty far!

2231
01:46:35,110 --> 01:46:40,210
We need to get a bit closer! Yeah! How do you lock on? Lock on!

2232
01:46:40,210 --> 01:46:43,710
Right, I wonder if we can lock on once we get closer...

2233
01:46:43,710 --> 01:46:45,410
Oh, you're right!

2234
01:46:45,410 --> 01:46:47,110
It says "lock"... Oh really?

2235
01:46:47,110 --> 01:46:51,110
Oh, I see... Hey! Why won't it come when we need it to, seriously!

2236
01:46:51,110 --> 01:46:53,310
Shoot it, Kanata!

2237
01:46:53,310 --> 01:46:56,810
I can't see it... something's...

2238
01:46:56,910 --> 01:46:58,430
It's pretty far.

2239
01:46:58,430 --> 01:47:00,730
It went off toward Yukino's place, huh.

2240
01:47:00,730 --> 01:47:01,950


2241
01:47:01,950 --> 01:47:02,890


2242
01:47:02,890 --> 01:47:04,190


2243
01:47:04,190 --> 01:47:04,950


2244
01:47:04,950 --> 01:47:05,950
What?! Are you kidding me?!

2245
01:47:05,950 --> 01:47:08,390
Why?!

2246
01:47:08,390 --> 01:47:09,270
Why?!

2247
01:47:09,270 --> 01:47:11,510
It was chasing us so hard just a moment ago!

2248
01:47:11,510 --> 01:47:14,170
Did I stab it with the sword?

2249
01:47:14,170 --> 01:47:19,080
It sensed the danger too.

2250
01:47:19,080 --> 01:47:24,290
Did it figure out we have homing missiles?

2251
01:47:25,670 --> 01:47:28,350
It knows us way too well.

2252
01:47:28,350 --> 01:47:29,590
It went completely the other way.

2253
01:47:29,590 --> 01:47:30,350
Is it just going to leave like this?

2254
01:47:30,350 --> 01:47:33,030
Oh! Oh! It suddenly came back!

2255
01:47:33,030 --> 01:47:34,070
Is it coming?

2256
01:47:34,070 --> 01:47:37,750
Based on the direction, I feel like it might come this way.

2257
01:47:37,750 --> 01:47:43,240
Laser!

2258
01:47:43,240 --> 01:47:45,280
Hey, seriously stop ghosting us, helicopter!

2259
01:47:45,280 --> 01:47:48,040
Oh, I can scope too.

2260
01:47:48,040 --> 01:47:55,140
Wow, you can hear it from that far away?

2261
01:48:00,120 --> 01:48:04,660
It's heading toward Water Treatment.

2262
01:48:04,660 --> 01:48:06,460
Where did the heli go?

2263
01:48:06,460 --> 01:48:08,460
Right now it's at G13.

2264
01:48:08,460 --> 01:48:10,260
That's really far.

2265
01:48:10,260 --> 01:48:12,060
What's going on?

2266
01:48:12,060 --> 01:48:13,060
It's not coming this way.

2267
01:48:13,060 --> 01:48:14,980
What's up?

2268
01:48:14,980 --> 01:48:15,860
It's scared.

2269
01:48:15,860 --> 01:48:16,860
Should we just wait at the house?

2270
01:48:16,860 --> 01:48:18,660
It's scared of us!

2271
01:48:18,660 --> 01:48:24,660
It suddenly got scared.

2272
01:48:24,660 --> 01:48:30,600
That's a nice angle of approach.

2273
01:48:30,600 --> 01:48:32,400
Got a bite!

2274
01:48:37,040 --> 01:48:39,640
Hmm, hmm, let me think...

2275
01:48:39,640 --> 01:48:42,640
Niko off-stream might get spooked again.

2276
01:48:42,640 --> 01:48:45,940
Where's the heli sound?

2277
01:48:45,940 --> 01:48:48,740
It's getting closer!

2278
01:48:48,740 --> 01:48:51,690
Ah, but the pin won't reach that far.

2279
01:48:51,690 --> 01:48:52,690
It's heading toward the dome!

2280
01:48:52,690 --> 01:48:56,490
How close does it need to be for it to work?

2281
01:48:56,490 --> 01:49:00,290
It's flying, but I think we'd need to be in about the same grid square.

2282
01:49:00,290 --> 01:49:03,290
Wait, isn't that super close?!

2283
01:49:03,290 --> 01:49:04,890
Nah, it's still far.

2284
01:49:04,890 --> 01:49:06,430
Did you shoot just now? That turn just now—

2285
01:49:06,430 --> 01:49:08,630
I took a shot but it's too far.

2286
01:49:08,630 --> 01:49:18,600
Yeah, a bit too far~

2287
01:49:18,600 --> 01:49:21,900
Come on, let me be the one chasing the heli now!

2288
01:49:21,900 --> 01:49:25,800
Now it's your turn to be chased! Brace yourself!

2289
01:49:25,800 --> 01:49:30,760
The lock-on is so strong though~

2290
01:49:30,760 --> 01:49:33,760
I wanna see it — the moment the missile fires~

2291
01:49:33,760 --> 01:49:35,460
Right, right~

2292
01:49:35,460 --> 01:49:38,820
Patrol helicopter...

2293
01:49:39,120 --> 01:49:41,120
Huh? What's that thing doing?

2294
01:49:41,120 --> 01:49:43,920
Wait, where'd it go?

2295
01:49:43,920 --> 01:49:47,730
It went off to the sea on the right.

2296
01:49:47,730 --> 01:49:49,730
What?

2297
01:49:49,730 --> 01:49:53,530
Oh, all the cars are gone now.

2298
01:49:53,530 --> 01:49:57,420
Seriously?

2299
01:49:57,420 --> 01:50:01,270
I was a little shaken when I saw that car was beyond repair.

2300
01:50:01,270 --> 01:50:03,890
I thought, wait, you can't fix this?

2301
01:50:03,890 --> 01:50:05,760
We got wrecked.

2302
01:50:05,760 --> 01:50:09,130
Wait, I can't even spot Polka on the map anymore.

2303
01:50:09,130 --> 01:50:12,310
Is it delivering something?

2304
01:50:12,310 --> 01:50:14,690
Does that mean it gave up? The heli?

2305
01:50:14,690 --> 01:50:17,030
Yeah, it's given up.

2306
01:50:17,030 --> 01:50:18,530
Looks like it — it stopped coming.

2307
01:50:18,530 --> 01:50:19,530
Phew~

2308
01:50:19,530 --> 01:50:22,130
Haah~

2309
01:50:22,130 --> 01:50:24,230
We still have the bicycle though.

2310
01:50:24,230 --> 01:50:28,230
Yeah, all we've got left is the bike — the bike and the horse.

2311
01:50:28,230 --> 01:50:30,230
Look on the bright side — at least we have the bike!

2312
01:50:31,050 --> 01:50:35,790
Well, there is a way to fully restore it, technically.

2313
01:50:35,790 --> 01:50:39,060
If you hammer away at it, it should fix, right?

2314
01:50:39,060 --> 01:50:41,090
Hmm, uh, yeah... I wonder.

2315
01:50:41,090 --> 01:50:43,390
Oh, nope, it won't fix — it's completely destroyed.

2316
01:50:43,390 --> 01:50:46,690
Right, the body itself is broken, so we'd have to find another one somewhere.

2317
01:50:46,690 --> 01:50:48,670
Yeah, this one's done for — it's broken.

2318
01:50:48,670 --> 01:50:52,780
It might have still been okay a little while ago.

2319
01:50:52,780 --> 01:50:57,910
Phew.

2320
01:50:57,910 --> 01:50:59,710
Well, that's that. So then—

2321
01:50:59,710 --> 01:51:01,230
They're gone.

2322
01:51:01,230 --> 01:51:06,990
If we do it at night, it'll be reduced. Yeah, right.

2323
01:51:06,990 --> 01:51:09,380
If we do it at night, it'll be less.

2324
01:51:09,380 --> 01:51:14,290
By the way, can you craft the homing missiles?

2325
01:51:14,290 --> 01:51:18,010
Hmm, good question.

2326
01:51:18,010 --> 01:51:28,010
Let me check if I can research it. I only have 9 homing missiles left anyway.

2327
01:51:28,550 --> 01:51:30,350
Only 9?

2328
01:51:30,350 --> 01:51:32,350
Well, 9 is still something.

2329
01:51:32,350 --> 01:51:37,260
This item can't be crafted from scrap.

2330
01:51:37,260 --> 01:51:39,260
Huh, really?

2331
01:51:39,260 --> 01:51:43,990
Even though it's a homing missile?

2332
01:51:43,990 --> 01:51:48,120
Do I have to craft it somewhere else?

2333
01:51:48,120 --> 01:51:50,920
Wait, is this a missile?

2334
01:51:50,920 --> 01:51:54,090
Which one is the homing one?

2335
01:51:54,090 --> 01:51:56,090
The one called homing missile.

2336
01:51:56,090 --> 01:51:57,590
The homing missile launcher is the one that needs a surveillance camera, right?

2337
01:51:57,590 --> 01:51:59,390
The one that requires a CCTV camera?

2338
01:51:59,390 --> 01:52:00,210
This one!

2339
01:52:00,210 --> 01:52:01,610
Yeah, yeah, that's the one!

2340
01:52:01,610 --> 01:52:04,870
Let me see if I can research the ammo with this.

2341
01:52:04,870 --> 01:52:10,860
Oh, it's already researched! I can craft it!

2342
01:52:10,860 --> 01:52:12,320
You already unlocked it? Nice!

2343
01:52:12,320 --> 01:52:14,320
Should I craft a bunch of them?

2344
01:52:14,320 --> 01:52:15,820
Yeah, do it!

2345
01:52:15,820 --> 01:52:21,310
We've really gone all out with the resources!

2346
01:52:21,310 --> 01:52:24,010
We gotta use them today for sure.

2347
01:52:24,010 --> 01:52:25,510
For real?

2348
01:52:25,510 --> 01:52:27,810
Pipes... are we using pipes again?

2349
01:52:27,810 --> 01:52:29,690
Pipes, gunpowder, junk...

2350
01:52:29,890 --> 01:52:33,490
Gunpowder, gunpowder... we're already running low on gunpowder.

2351
01:52:33,490 --> 01:52:36,300
Gunpowder, gunpowder, gunpowder, junk...

2352
01:52:36,300 --> 01:52:40,380
I'll craft the homing missiles.

2353
01:52:40,380 --> 01:52:42,180
Homing missiles.

2354
01:52:42,180 --> 01:52:44,980
They say 9 is enough, though.

2355
01:52:44,980 --> 01:52:49,020
But I'd rather craft the launcher too.

2356
01:52:49,020 --> 01:52:51,020
Yeah, the launcher...

2357
01:52:51,020 --> 01:52:54,820
Yeah, I really want the launcher.

2358
01:52:54,820 --> 01:52:56,820
We need to find a camera first.

2359
01:52:56,820 --> 01:52:59,700
Can we get to the beach?

2360
01:52:59,700 --> 01:53:04,800
The fact that we've gotten to the point of crafting a launcher is kind of scary, honestly.

2361
01:53:04,800 --> 01:53:07,760
The one that drops, right?

2362
01:53:07,760 --> 01:53:11,220
We might need a CCTV launcher for it.

2363
01:53:11,220 --> 01:53:15,220
I never even thought about crafting a launcher before.

2364
01:53:15,220 --> 01:53:18,840
Should be fine.

2365
01:53:18,840 --> 01:53:26,820
This is a hatch, right?

2366
01:53:28,920 --> 01:53:32,420
Kanata's place too... what should I do? I already tidied up.

2367
01:53:32,420 --> 01:53:37,680
Oh, maybe the shop sells it!

2368
01:53:37,680 --> 01:53:40,580
CCTV.

2369
01:53:40,580 --> 01:53:43,160
I wonder what the most expensive thing you can buy at the shop is.

2370
01:53:43,160 --> 01:53:47,620
Probably a helicopter or something?

2371
01:53:47,620 --> 01:53:48,640
A helicopter?

2372
01:53:48,640 --> 01:53:50,120
A large helicopter.

2373
01:53:50,120 --> 01:53:50,740
CCTV camera.

2374
01:53:58,780 --> 01:54:02,400
I'm riding a large helicopter.

2375
01:54:02,400 --> 01:54:05,480
Not here?

2376
01:54:05,480 --> 01:54:11,350
Do I have to go all the way to the casino?

2377
01:54:11,350 --> 01:54:14,750
Well, we do have a helicopter though.

2378
01:54:14,750 --> 01:54:18,620
We have a helicopter, but...

2379
01:54:18,620 --> 01:54:19,620
We have a helicopter.

2380
01:54:19,620 --> 01:54:22,620
We have a helicopter.

2381
01:54:22,620 --> 01:54:26,220
No CCTV camera.

2382
01:54:26,220 --> 01:54:26,820
Not here, huh.

2383
01:54:26,820 --> 01:54:27,820
They don't sell it.

2384
01:54:30,340 --> 01:54:32,300
What about your helicopter?

2385
01:54:32,300 --> 01:54:36,520
The helicopter... landing it is pretty tricky.

2386
01:54:36,520 --> 01:54:39,140
Oh! If you take the helicopter, it'd be super fast!

2387
01:54:39,140 --> 01:54:44,280
I know, but I don't really want to ride it...

2388
01:54:44,280 --> 01:54:48,240
It'd be so quick by helicopter, why not?

2389
01:54:48,240 --> 01:54:52,460
For travel, it's either a bike, a horse, or the helicopter.

2390
01:54:52,460 --> 01:54:59,340
Just fly there by helicopter, easy!

2391
01:55:00,970 --> 01:55:03,770
Ugh, landing is so hard though.

2392
01:55:03,770 --> 01:55:06,580
Not my problem, Polka!

2393
01:55:06,580 --> 01:55:08,570
Why don't you try riding it too, Bob?

2394
01:55:08,570 --> 01:55:11,370
If you crash and break it, just so you know...

2395
01:55:11,370 --> 01:55:15,140
It's fine, we have 5000 scrap.

2396
01:55:15,140 --> 01:55:18,850
Wow, then practice, Luna!

2397
01:55:18,850 --> 01:55:22,850
Practice a lot, and when morning comes, let's ride it.

2398
01:55:22,850 --> 01:55:25,650
It's the feel of flying, you know.

2399
01:55:25,650 --> 01:55:28,940
Practice, practice!

2400
01:55:28,940 --> 01:55:32,940
It takes a bit of fuel though.

2401
01:55:35,360 --> 01:55:43,510
This definitely won't fit, but I put it in anyway

2402
01:55:46,540 --> 01:55:48,380
The heli stopped coming

2403
01:55:48,180 --> 01:55:49,980
The heli already left

2404
01:55:49,980 --> 01:55:51,980
And then it spawned again

2405
01:55:51,980 --> 01:55:53,980
The heli was there until we said hi

2406
01:55:53,980 --> 01:55:55,780
Why does the heli always...

2407
01:55:55,780 --> 01:55:57,580
It was so sudden, right?

2408
01:55:57,580 --> 01:55:59,580
Right when we were about to give up

2409
01:55:59,580 --> 01:56:01,580
and said "let's do this"

2410
01:56:01,580 --> 01:56:03,380
that thing...

2411
01:56:03,380 --> 01:56:04,380
I hate it

2412
01:56:04,380 --> 01:56:05,380
That's so typical

2413
01:56:05,380 --> 01:56:06,380
Seriously

2414
01:56:06,380 --> 01:56:07,380
Right?

2415
01:56:07,380 --> 01:56:10,180
It's such a flip-flopper

2416
01:56:10,180 --> 01:56:19,000
We could also build a car from scratch

2417
01:56:19,000 --> 01:56:22,460
It got a bit weathered

2418
01:56:22,460 --> 01:56:27,330
The wind, huh...

2419
01:56:27,330 --> 01:56:31,960
Are we taking the heli?

2420
01:56:31,960 --> 01:56:33,960
Aren't we riding the heli?

2421
01:56:33,960 --> 01:56:35,760
Where are we going?

2422
01:56:36,560 --> 01:56:38,960
I don't know if we can go, but...

2423
01:56:38,960 --> 01:56:41,360
If we're riding it, where was it again...

2424
01:56:41,360 --> 01:56:42,860
If we're going...

2425
01:56:42,860 --> 01:56:45,260
What was it again, um...

2426
01:56:45,260 --> 01:56:46,660
That's scary

2427
01:56:46,660 --> 01:56:48,160
The casino, right?

2428
01:56:48,160 --> 01:56:52,290
Going shopping

2429
01:56:52,290 --> 01:56:56,190
This is at a tricky angle

2430
01:56:56,190 --> 01:56:59,090
There's a chance we fall, you know

2431
01:56:59,090 --> 01:57:01,790
Oh, is Kanatan going to clear the way?

2432
01:57:01,790 --> 01:57:04,090
Oh, think we can do a po-po?

2433
01:57:04,090 --> 01:57:05,360
Yeah, we can't

2434
01:57:05,360 --> 01:57:12,500
I was wondering what we'd do — worth a try though

2435
01:57:12,500 --> 01:57:18,540
We can't, but should I not bring the M249?

2436
01:57:18,540 --> 01:57:25,280
Leave it at home? We might fall

2437
01:57:25,280 --> 01:57:31,600
Okay

2438
01:57:31,600 --> 01:57:37,170
Just getting it out is hard — push push push

2439
01:57:37,170 --> 01:57:39,100
Push, push push push

2440
01:57:39,100 --> 01:57:42,060
Okay, now controlling it while riding

2441
01:57:42,060 --> 01:57:44,060
Whoa~

2442
01:57:44,060 --> 01:57:48,010
Which side do I put this on again?

2443
01:57:48,010 --> 01:57:51,520
Oh, there was no fuel

2444
01:57:51,520 --> 01:57:55,280
Add fuel, then get on

2445
01:57:55,280 --> 01:57:57,160
Oh?

2446
01:57:57,160 --> 01:58:01,620
With the controller

2447
01:58:01,620 --> 01:58:06,220
Oh, ohhhhhhh!

2448
01:58:07,300 --> 01:58:08,300
Ohh

2449
01:58:08,300 --> 01:58:09,860


2450
01:58:09,860 --> 01:58:12,040
I can see an airdrop

2451
01:58:12,040 --> 01:58:14,220
Okay

2452
01:58:14,220 --> 01:58:15,900
Nothing?

2453
01:58:15,900 --> 01:58:17,600
Don't just say okay

2454
01:58:17,600 --> 01:58:20,180
When flying, um, double...

2455
01:58:20,180 --> 01:58:22,540
How do you go up again?

2456
01:58:22,540 --> 01:58:24,860
Hold double to go up?

2457
01:58:24,860 --> 01:58:28,560
Wait, I can break it? Or do I drive it now?

2458
01:58:28,560 --> 01:58:31,040
Okay then, you drive

2459
01:58:31,040 --> 01:58:33,040
Let's gooo!

2460
01:58:33,040 --> 01:58:35,540
I've been waiting for this!

2461
01:58:35,540 --> 01:58:39,440
Wait, I thought I left the M249 behind but I still have it

2462
01:58:39,440 --> 01:58:44,110
Let me give it to Kanatan

2463
01:58:44,110 --> 01:58:45,310
No wait...

2464
01:58:45,310 --> 01:58:47,110
Did I put down the wrong thing?

2465
01:58:47,110 --> 01:58:50,110
Let me store it with Kanatan — the M249

2466
01:58:50,110 --> 01:58:53,910
This is the M249, okay

2467
01:58:53,910 --> 01:58:58,190
Here

2468
01:58:58,190 --> 01:59:01,120
Hah

2469
01:59:01,920 --> 01:59:02,920
Alright then

2470
01:59:02,920 --> 01:59:06,040
Is it here?

2471
01:59:06,040 --> 01:59:07,340
Uh, yeah

2472
01:59:07,340 --> 01:59:09,340
No, the casino, the casino

2473
01:59:09,340 --> 01:59:10,900
Roughly...

2474
01:59:10,900 --> 01:59:12,600
I forgot how to do it

2475
01:59:12,600 --> 01:59:13,980
Isn't it straight ahead?

2476
01:59:13,980 --> 01:59:15,980
Where's the casino?

2477
01:59:15,980 --> 01:59:18,200
Bandit Camp

2478
01:59:18,200 --> 01:59:21,410
Oh, wait, hold on

2479
01:59:21,410 --> 01:59:23,610
What the—!?

2480
01:59:23,610 --> 01:59:26,070
The blades, the blades hit something

2481
01:59:26,070 --> 01:59:30,870
Roughly heading north now

2482
01:59:30,870 --> 01:59:32,730
Oh! Nice! Nice!

2483
01:59:32,730 --> 01:59:35,750
Wow, you're really good at this, Hime!

2484
01:59:35,750 --> 01:59:39,270
I can only go up though

2485
01:59:39,270 --> 01:59:41,750
Going up is important! But keep it straight

2486
01:59:41,750 --> 01:59:43,450
Wonderful!

2487
01:59:43,450 --> 01:59:44,650
The angle looks good too

2488
01:59:44,650 --> 01:59:46,310
Ah, keep it level

2489
01:59:46,310 --> 01:59:47,450
Hey, you're going backwards?

2490
01:59:47,450 --> 01:59:48,450
You're going backwards, Hime?

2491
01:59:48,450 --> 01:59:51,790
You need to go forward, lean forward

2492
01:59:51,790 --> 01:59:53,550
I can do the posture though

2493
01:59:53,550 --> 01:59:56,190
Hmm...

2494
01:59:56,190 --> 01:59:58,250
You're doing great, Hime

2495
01:59:59,210 --> 02:00:05,620
I can see the airdrop clearly too

2496
02:00:05,620 --> 02:00:08,060
The flying part looks good

2497
02:00:08,060 --> 02:00:09,260
Landing is scary

2498
02:00:09,260 --> 02:00:10,400
Landing is scary?

2499
02:00:10,400 --> 02:00:12,220
Landing is scary

2500
02:00:12,220 --> 02:00:16,020
Takeoff and landing are the most dangerous parts of flying

2501
02:00:16,020 --> 02:00:18,080
That's true

2502
02:00:18,080 --> 02:00:21,620
But aren't you doing well?

2503
02:00:21,620 --> 02:00:23,480
Really?

2504
02:00:23,480 --> 02:00:24,560
Yeah

2505
02:00:24,560 --> 02:00:29,800
Wait, where did you learn this? Isn't this amazing?

2506
02:00:29,800 --> 02:00:31,460
Self-taught

2507
02:00:31,460 --> 02:00:33,520
Isn't that incredible? Aren't you good at this?

2508
02:00:33,520 --> 02:00:38,280
But...

2509
02:00:38,280 --> 02:00:40,120
Where is it?

2510
02:00:40,120 --> 02:00:41,340
Getting closer

2511
02:00:41,340 --> 02:00:45,930
Where should I land?

2512
02:00:45,930 --> 02:00:49,450
What's the safe zone? Will I get shot down by the patrol helicopter?

2513
02:00:49,450 --> 02:00:52,350
Apparently you won't get shot down here

2514
02:00:52,350 --> 02:00:54,790
Then something like this should be fine, right?

2515
02:00:56,170 --> 02:00:58,030
Oh, how did it come out?

2516
02:00:58,030 --> 02:00:59,470
Ohhh

2517
02:00:59,470 --> 02:01:03,410
Oh nice nice nice nice! Oh amazing amazing amazing! Oh!

2518
02:01:03,410 --> 02:01:05,370
So smooth!

2519
02:01:05,370 --> 02:01:08,590
Okay! Whoa! Oh, huh?

2520
02:01:08,590 --> 02:01:13,060
That was scary

2521
02:01:13,060 --> 02:01:15,860
It's fine, this can be fixed, no problem

2522
02:01:15,860 --> 02:01:18,260
Did you hit a rock? Yeah

2523
02:01:18,260 --> 02:01:21,860
That rock is to blame! The rock's fault! It shouldn't be there, it shouldn't be there!

2524
02:01:21,860 --> 02:01:24,850
You did great, you did great!

2525
02:01:25,460 --> 02:01:25,960
Huh?

2526
02:01:25,960 --> 02:01:28,060
It broke a bit but it's fine

2527
02:01:28,060 --> 02:01:28,940
Seriously?

2528
02:01:28,940 --> 02:01:30,160
It's fine, it's fine

2529
02:01:30,160 --> 02:01:31,920
That was, you know, that kind of...

2530
02:01:31,920 --> 02:01:32,840
What do you call it?

2531
02:01:32,840 --> 02:01:34,340
Yeah, a performance

2532
02:01:34,340 --> 02:01:37,260
That was a performance, see

2533
02:01:37,260 --> 02:01:37,940
It's totally clean, right?

2534
02:01:37,940 --> 02:01:38,900
It's within the rocks

2535
02:01:38,900 --> 02:01:39,400
Yeah

2536
02:01:39,400 --> 02:01:42,400
Oh, it's fine, it's fixed

2537
02:01:42,400 --> 02:01:43,860
Amazing!

2538
02:01:43,860 --> 02:01:46,160
Oh, we managed somehow

2539
02:01:46,160 --> 02:01:48,860
"We managed somehow"? You...

2540
02:01:48,860 --> 02:01:50,460
So many things...

2541
02:01:50,460 --> 02:01:53,020
You've grown so much!

2542
02:01:53,020 --> 02:01:58,100
Man, this Rust session...

2543
02:01:58,100 --> 02:02:02,580
It's been a story of trying all kinds of things

2544
02:02:02,580 --> 02:02:05,120
All over the place

2545
02:02:05,120 --> 02:02:10,420
Do you have any security cameras? — I told you they don't sell them

2546
02:02:10,420 --> 02:02:12,720
Don't you have any? — I told you they don't sell them

2547
02:02:12,720 --> 02:02:16,900
Not buying what they don't have — Do they secretly sell them?

2548
02:02:18,930 --> 02:02:23,870
They don't have it — You can't buy what doesn't exist

2549
02:02:23,870 --> 02:02:28,890
Nothing here — What did I come here for again?

2550
02:02:28,890 --> 02:02:33,630
I wonder if they sell security cameras — They probably don't, right?

2551
02:02:33,630 --> 02:02:38,690
Maybe I missed it — There might be something

2552
02:02:38,690 --> 02:02:45,270
Nobody's here — I've never tried to buy a security camera before

2553
02:02:45,630 --> 02:02:52,020
Hey — Since you never bought one, you still don't have one

2554
02:02:52,020 --> 02:02:56,860
Nothing here — Maybe they just don't have it

2555
02:02:56,860 --> 02:03:01,140
What about Polka's practice helicopter? — Oh!

2556
02:03:01,140 --> 02:03:03,480
Do you have money?

2557
02:03:03,480 --> 02:03:08,180
I brought 2800 scrap so I can buy it — Buy it

2558
02:03:08,180 --> 02:03:11,540
Pol-pol, over here — Hmm

2559
02:03:11,540 --> 02:03:13,340
Wolf

2560
02:03:13,340 --> 02:03:16,340
Wow, that's nostalgic

2561
02:03:16,340 --> 02:03:18,140
Huh? Gunshots?

2562
02:03:18,140 --> 02:03:19,940
Eh, it's fine, it's fine

2563
02:03:19,940 --> 02:03:21,740
Same old, same old

2564
02:03:21,740 --> 02:03:23,740
You can buy it here

2565
02:03:23,740 --> 02:03:24,740
There we go

2566
02:03:24,740 --> 02:03:25,540
You could buy

2567
02:03:25,540 --> 02:03:27,340
some other stuff too, you know

2568
02:03:27,340 --> 02:03:31,140
Let's see... aircraft...

2569
02:03:31,140 --> 02:03:32,140
The smallest helicopter?

2570
02:03:32,140 --> 02:03:33,940
Mini heli

2571
02:03:33,940 --> 02:03:34,910
750

2572
02:03:34,910 --> 02:03:36,540
Thank you

2573
02:03:36,540 --> 02:03:38,540
Riding a heli is crazy though

2574
02:03:38,540 --> 02:03:39,100
Yeah

2575
02:03:39,340 --> 02:03:41,200
Wanna try? It's scary though

2576
02:03:41,200 --> 02:03:44,140
Teach me how

2577
02:03:44,140 --> 02:03:49,120
So, you want to move the mouse really slowly

2578
02:03:49,120 --> 02:03:51,180
First, how do you even make it go up?

2579
02:03:51,180 --> 02:03:57,780
Press W to start the engine, hold W to go up, S to go down

2580
02:03:57,780 --> 02:04:02,540
Then use A or D to change direction

2581
02:04:02,540 --> 02:04:07,480
And use the mouse to keep it level — tilt forward

2582
02:04:07,480 --> 02:04:13,080
Moving the mouse up tilts you forward

2583
02:04:13,080 --> 02:04:19,660
It's going up like crazy

2584
02:04:19,660 --> 02:04:21,440
Okay I went up, now what?

2585
02:04:21,440 --> 02:04:30,140
To move forward, push the mouse up a little and you'll go forward

2586
02:04:30,140 --> 02:04:35,040
If you're going backward, it means you're pulling the mouse down

2587
02:04:35,040 --> 02:04:36,600
Push it up

2588
02:04:36,600 --> 02:04:38,220
Push it up

2589
02:04:38,220 --> 02:04:41,640
What are you even saying

2590
02:04:41,640 --> 02:04:44,840
Well, you just have to

2591
02:04:44,840 --> 02:04:46,200
get a feel for it

2592
02:04:46,200 --> 02:04:49,280
Tilt it a little

2593
02:04:49,280 --> 02:04:50,840
Which direction is this?

2594
02:04:50,840 --> 02:04:53,740
This way?

2595
02:04:53,740 --> 02:04:56,970
But somehow

2596
02:04:56,970 --> 02:04:58,770
it looks like you're doing okay

2597
02:04:58,770 --> 02:04:59,830
I'm going backward

2598
02:04:59,830 --> 02:05:02,290
What do I do when I'm going backward?

2599
02:05:02,290 --> 02:05:05,220
Push the mouse up — flick it up

2600
02:05:05,220 --> 02:05:07,090
Flick it and you'll go forward a lot

2601
02:05:07,090 --> 02:05:09,810
I'm going backward! When I flick it—

2602
02:05:09,810 --> 02:05:11,690
Mouse up — UP, I said up!

2603
02:05:11,690 --> 02:05:16,290
What do you mean up? I'm going backward!

2604
02:05:16,290 --> 02:05:19,590
I'm telling you, mouse up!

2605
02:05:19,590 --> 02:05:20,590
Flick it, flick it

2606
02:05:20,590 --> 02:05:21,390
Flick

2607
02:05:21,390 --> 02:05:22,190
Up — flick it

2608
02:05:22,190 --> 02:05:23,990
Huh? Up — wait, what?

2609
02:05:23,990 --> 02:05:25,990
When I go up, I go backward, right?

2610
02:05:25,990 --> 02:05:27,790
Is it the opposite?

2611
02:05:27,790 --> 02:05:29,590
Did I get it wrong?

2612
02:05:30,390 --> 02:05:33,070
Pull it toward you — toward you!

2613
02:05:33,070 --> 02:05:33,990
Toward me?

2614
02:05:33,990 --> 02:05:35,940
It was the opposite

2615
02:05:35,940 --> 02:05:40,130
Wait, but I'm still going backward

2616
02:05:40,130 --> 02:05:42,080
I can't really explain it without being on it myself

2617
02:05:42,080 --> 02:05:42,880
Huh?

2618
02:05:42,880 --> 02:05:43,880
Was it backward?

2619
02:05:43,880 --> 02:05:46,680
Wait, wait, too close, too close, hold on

2620
02:05:46,680 --> 02:05:49,480
Everything is too close — the ground!

2621
02:05:49,480 --> 02:05:50,480
Where did it go?

2622
02:05:50,480 --> 02:05:52,280
She crashed!

2623
02:05:52,280 --> 02:05:54,280
Polka crashed!

2624
02:05:54,280 --> 02:05:56,280
Polka crashed?

2625
02:05:56,280 --> 02:05:59,450
What happened?

2626
02:06:01,050 --> 02:06:03,230
Where even is this~?

2627
02:06:03,230 --> 02:06:04,890
Hehehe

2628
02:06:04,890 --> 02:06:06,330
How far did Polka fly?

2629
02:06:06,330 --> 02:06:09,490
Whoa, she flew pretty far out

2630
02:06:09,490 --> 02:06:10,990
She ended up way up north

2631
02:06:10,990 --> 02:06:13,470
I'm bad at going forward in this thing

2632
02:06:13,470 --> 02:06:15,570
How do you even go forward?

2633
02:06:15,570 --> 02:06:18,370
And she survived somehow

2634
02:06:18,370 --> 02:06:23,490
Right, it's hard to explain without actually being on it

2635
02:06:23,490 --> 02:06:25,350
I'm bad at going forward

2636
02:06:25,350 --> 02:06:26,890
I keep going backward

2637
02:06:26,890 --> 02:06:29,590
Wait, Polka didn't die from that?

2638
02:06:29,790 --> 02:06:36,180
I thought I was getting a bit close to the ground

2639
02:06:36,180 --> 02:06:39,500
You probably hit Space and died normally

2640
02:06:39,500 --> 02:06:41,620
Oh, I see — I accidentally hit Space

2641
02:06:41,620 --> 02:06:44,540
It's on fire! Good, at least we're not bothering anyone else's base.

2642
02:06:44,540 --> 02:06:47,720
Well, but...

2643
02:06:47,720 --> 02:06:55,840
Like, I don't really get what "push the mouse forward" means.

2644
02:06:55,840 --> 02:07:01,040
Does "forward" mean pull it toward you, or push it away?

2645
02:07:02,220 --> 02:07:03,620
Push it away?

2646
02:07:03,620 --> 02:07:06,780
Wait, where did I put Shelly?

2647
02:07:06,780 --> 02:07:10,630
There it is!

2648
02:07:10,630 --> 02:07:11,590
Push it forward?

2649
02:07:11,590 --> 02:07:14,170
Even when I push it forward, like...

2650
02:07:14,170 --> 02:07:14,970
Where's the effect?

2651
02:07:14,970 --> 02:07:16,710
It just doesn't work right.

2652
02:07:16,710 --> 02:07:19,610
Maybe I'm not keeping it level?

2653
02:07:19,610 --> 02:07:29,050
So W makes you go up...

2654
02:07:29,050 --> 02:07:31,730
And if you tilt the mouse upward like this...

2655
02:07:31,730 --> 02:07:33,930
You should move forward.

2656
02:07:33,930 --> 02:07:35,730
Like this... hngh.

2657
02:07:35,730 --> 02:07:41,990
Where's Popo?

2658
02:07:41,990 --> 02:07:51,990
Going backward is probably because the mouse is sliding downward.

2659
02:07:53,840 --> 02:07:56,940
Do I need to keep pushing it more and more forward?

2660
02:07:56,940 --> 02:08:06,140
Just a little is enough, right? It's fast... like... yeah.

2661
02:08:06,140 --> 02:08:10,940
I kept telling myself "just a little," but then somehow...

2662
02:08:10,940 --> 02:08:14,180
I kept drifting further and further back, didn't I?

2663
02:08:14,180 --> 02:08:16,700
Ugh, this is so hard!

2664
02:08:16,700 --> 02:08:18,200
This is genuinely difficult.

2665
02:08:18,200 --> 02:08:21,380
It's really hard! Polka has never once gotten it right!

2666
02:08:21,380 --> 02:08:22,540
With the helicopter...

2667
02:08:22,540 --> 02:08:29,490
Could they be coming to pick me up...? Whoooa, that's amazing!!

2668
02:08:29,490 --> 02:08:30,600
Coming to pick me up...

2669
02:08:30,600 --> 02:08:33,100
Someone came to pick me up in a helicopter!

2670
02:08:33,100 --> 02:08:35,500
In a heli... they came by heli!

2671
02:08:35,500 --> 02:08:40,840
Where is this?

2672
02:08:41,080 --> 02:08:42,880
Whoa, over here!

2673
02:08:42,880 --> 02:08:44,880
Whoa, there it is!

2674
02:08:44,880 --> 02:08:45,880
Around here.

2675
02:08:45,880 --> 02:08:50,680
The people who are good at this are amazing~

2676
02:08:50,680 --> 02:08:56,070
What's a battle heli? Does it shoot missiles?

2677
02:08:56,070 --> 02:08:59,270
A battle heli sounds super hard.

2678
02:08:59,270 --> 02:09:00,070
I wonder what it's like.

2679
02:09:00,070 --> 02:09:03,670
But there was a heli that could carry a lot of people, right?

2680
02:09:03,670 --> 02:09:05,170
The one that fits a bunch of people.

2681
02:09:05,170 --> 02:09:08,720
We were almost there.

2682
02:09:09,220 --> 02:09:13,340
It's okay to lean forward quite a bit, right?

2683
02:09:13,340 --> 02:09:15,500
No, that's amazing.

2684
02:09:15,500 --> 02:09:18,680
Oh, oh, oh! Wow, so good, so good, so good!

2685
02:09:18,680 --> 02:09:21,780
Hime, I genuinely think you're amazing at this.

2686
02:09:21,780 --> 02:09:24,560
In just a few tries, this cleanly...

2687
02:09:24,560 --> 02:09:26,920
Being able to do that is incredible.

2688
02:09:26,920 --> 02:09:28,160
Heh~

2689
02:09:28,160 --> 02:09:30,080
Want to drive again?

2690
02:09:30,080 --> 02:09:32,640
Yeah, dying here would be for nothing.

2691
02:09:32,640 --> 02:09:34,180
All the way out here...

2692
02:09:34,180 --> 02:09:36,380
If both of us die here...

2693
02:09:36,620 --> 02:09:38,620
That'd be terrible.

2694
02:09:38,620 --> 02:09:40,800
Swoosh~

2695
02:09:40,800 --> 02:09:42,540
Let's head back.

2696
02:09:42,540 --> 02:09:46,340
OK, so the location is...

2697
02:09:46,340 --> 02:09:48,340
This blue one over here.

2698
02:09:48,340 --> 02:09:52,030
Yay!

2699
02:09:52,030 --> 02:09:55,050
With the controller...

2700
02:09:55,050 --> 02:09:58,050
To the left?

2701
02:09:58,050 --> 02:10:00,610
Alright, ascending!

2702
02:10:01,570 --> 02:10:03,570


2703
02:10:03,570 --> 02:10:07,110
I can see the whole world!

2704
02:10:07,110 --> 02:10:09,660
Hmm~

2705
02:10:09,660 --> 02:10:14,020
I can see the ground...

2706
02:10:14,020 --> 02:10:17,900
You can see it!

2707
02:10:17,900 --> 02:10:19,900
Hey!

2708
02:10:19,900 --> 02:10:22,260
Slide upward and move forward...

2709
02:10:22,260 --> 02:10:28,260
Ah, this is the feeling, right? Just a tiny bit forward — whoa, amazing!

2710
02:10:28,260 --> 02:10:31,950
Come on!

2711
02:10:32,550 --> 02:10:39,330
Heli!

2712
02:10:39,330 --> 02:10:43,840
Heli!

2713
02:10:43,840 --> 02:10:46,640
More, get a little closer.

2714
02:10:46,640 --> 02:10:51,510
There, go!

2715
02:10:51,510 --> 02:10:55,170
Like, just enough to move around up there.

2716
02:10:55,170 --> 02:10:57,760
That's incredible.

2717
02:10:57,760 --> 02:10:59,710
You're amazing, Hime.

2718
02:10:59,710 --> 02:11:01,710
I thought you could only go slowly.

2719
02:11:01,710 --> 02:11:06,470
That's amazing.

2720
02:11:06,470 --> 02:11:13,630
You can see all kinds of structures on this map.

2721
02:11:13,630 --> 02:11:16,470
You can tell there were tons of them around the gambling area.

2722
02:11:16,470 --> 02:11:19,170
There are a lot of them around here.

2723
02:11:19,170 --> 02:11:26,620
There were so many around the gambling spot.

2724
02:11:29,650 --> 02:11:32,030
We were flying pretty high earlier, weren't we?

2725
02:11:32,030 --> 02:11:38,690
Yeah, yeah, flying — or more like floating, I guess.

2726
02:11:38,690 --> 02:11:42,290
But we're going the complete opposite direction from where I thought, so again...

2727
02:11:42,290 --> 02:11:43,090
Oh wait, I overstated that.

2728
02:11:43,090 --> 02:11:45,090
Oh, oh, oh, the base—

2729
02:11:45,090 --> 02:11:46,690
